        Release(version: "2.20 (99)", date: "27 November 2026", headline: "Progress gets eight colour tiles and a pinned row to jump between its parts, and Garmin cards that were empty now fill in", items: [
            "Progress · New: eight colour tiles at the top. Before: Progress was one long page; to reach Routes or Your bests you scrolled past everything above. Now: right under the Progress title there are eight tiles, each in its own colour with a live figure: Race (weeks or days to go), Fitness (your fitness number from Fitness and freshness), Load (hours trained this week), Zones (zone 2 time this week, a dash until Garmin has answered), Routes (outdoor routes this month), Kept (sessions done of those due so far), Bests (how many personal bests) and Month (the month in review). Tap a tile and the page scrolls to that part. iPhone shows two columns of tiles; iPad on its side and the Mac show four.",
            "Progress · New: a pinned row of chips. Before: once you had scrolled down you had to scroll all the way back up to jump somewhere else. Now: when the tiles have scrolled out of sight, a slim row of the same colour chips stays at the top of the page. The part you are looking at lights up as a filled chip and the others stay pale. Tap a chip to jump to that part. Scroll back to the top and the row goes away, because the tiles are there again.",
            "Progress · New: each part shows where it starts. Before: the cards of the different parts looked alike. Now: the first card of each part has a strip of the part's colour along its top edge.",
            "Progress · Fixed: the Time in zones · this week card now appears. Before (since 2.8): the card never showed on any device, because it only asked Garmin once it was already on screen, so it never was. Now: Progress asks Garmin for it when it opens, at most once every 30 minutes.",
            "Garmin · Fixed: Garmin readings that run at the same time no longer knock each other out. Before: when Garmin turned one reading away, the app threw away the new pass that the others had just fetched, so several cards failed one after another. Now: one turned-away reading fetches one new pass, and the others keep it.",
            "Progress · Fixed: Fitter at the same pulse said the wrong thing when Garmin was silent. Before: it said Not enough steady runs or rides at your zone 2 pulse yet, although in truth Garmin had not answered. Now: it says Garmin did not answer just now. Tap to try again., the same words as the Routes card. A reading that failed is also tried again after 2 minutes, instead of after 30.",
            "Fixed: three more places had the same hidden fault as the zones card (they only asked for their numbers once they were already showing). Before: a done session's score came only for this week's sessions; the gym block on a strength session came only after Body had been opened; the race report would never have read Garmin after the race. Now: each one asks when its page opens.",
            "Signs · Changed: new signs, listed in Signs in this app. A colour tile is one part of Progress; tap it to jump there. In the pinned row a filled chip is the part on screen now and pale chips are the other parts.",
            "Unchanged: everything else on Progress, your plan, your numbers, Garmin keys and iCloud. The tiles only show and jump; they change nothing.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Progress (the top of the page, the pinned row, Time in zones, Fitter at the same pulse) and Signs in this app (Progress).",
