        Release(version: "2.19.3 (98)", date: "27 November 2026", headline: "Routes on the Mac: Done works, the map frames your usual area, and Garmin answers more reliably", items: [
            "Routes · Fixed: Done on the Mac. Before (2.19): on the Mac, Done did not close the Routes page, and Escape did not either. Now: Done and Escape close it, on every device (iPhone, iPad and Mac).",
            "Garmin · Fixed: Garmin answers more reliably. Before: when several parts of the app asked Garmin at the same moment (for example when you open Progress: the Routes card, Fitter at the same pulse and the zones card), each one fetched its own Garmin pass, and a newer pass made the older one invalid. So some of those requests failed and their cards stayed empty; the Routes card even said No outdoor sessions this month yet although there were many. Now: they share one pass, fetched once, so the cards fill in together.",
            "Routes · Changed: the words on the Routes card. Before: while the routes were still being fetched, or when Garmin did not answer, the card said No outdoor sessions this month yet. Now: it says Reading your routes… while it fetches; Garmin did not answer just now. Tap to try again. when the read failed (a tap opens the map page, which tries again); and No outdoor sessions this month yet. only when Garmin answered and the month really has none. The Routes page says the same three lines.",
            "Routes · Changed: where the map looks first. Before: the map zoomed out to fit every route of the month, so one far-away hike (50 km away, invented) shrank all your usual routes to a dot. Now: the map first frames the area where most of your routes are (routes whose middle is within 25 km of the middle of the month's routes, when that is at least half of them). The far-away ones are still drawn: move or zoom the map to see them. The card's small map does the same.",
            "Unchanged: everything else. Your plan, the chips, the month, the plate on a tapped route, Garmin keys and iCloud are untouched.",
