        Release(version: "2.19 (95)", date: "27 November 2026", headline: "Routes on a map, your own sleep need, gym time instead of kilograms, a gym session on any day, and the Extra workout pill moved", items: [
            "Routes · New: Progress › Routes. Before: a route showed only on the page of one done outdoor session. Now: a card ROUTES on Progress with this month's outdoor routes from Garmin on a small map, each sport in its own colour, and a line like 12 routes · 5 runs · 6 rides · 1 hike (invented). Tap it for the Routes page: a full map you can move and zoom, the month at the top with ‹ › to go back and forward, chips Run, Bike, Swim and Hike in their colours (filled = shown, outlined = hidden), and a small plate when you tap a route: the day, Garmin's name, the distance in km and the time. Done closes it; on the Mac Escape does.",
            "Routes · Good to know: what counts. Outdoor means runs, rides, open-water swims, hikes and walks with a GPS track. A treadmill run, an indoor ride, a pool swim and the gym are not on the map. Routes come from Garmin, so it needs your Garmin key on that device; without it the card says Routes come from Garmin. Add your Garmin key in Settings › Garmin. Up to 20 new routes are read on each visit, with a line like Reading 4 of 12 routes…, and each route is kept on the device, so it is read only once. Unchanged: the route on a done outdoor session's own page (since 2.8).",
            "Sleep need · New: Settings › Garmin › Sleep need. Before: Body › Sleep debt counted each night against Garmin's own sleep-need estimate, often about 8h, and the sheet said Need about 8h a night. Now: a row Sleep need right under the Garmin row, with the grey line 6h a night — your setting (or Garmin's estimate). Its page offers Garmin's estimate, 5h, 5h 30m, 6h, 6h 30m, 7h, 7h 30m, 8h, 8h 30m and 9h, with a tick beside the chosen one, and Cancel and a green Save (Escape is Cancel on the Mac). It starts at 6h, as you asked, and is the same on every device, kept in your iCloud with the app's other shared settings. With 6h set, every night counts against 6h and the sheet says Need 6h a night (your setting). Choosing Garmin's estimate brings back the old way.",
            "Body · Changed: Gym sessions show time, not kilograms. Before: the card's big figure was the kilograms lifted (like 3,250 kg), every row of the list showed kg, the line vs the one before had a kg part (+2 sets · −17 min · +640 kg), and the gym block on a strength session's page ended with the kg. Now: the big figure is the session's time (like 1h 05m); the line under it is the day and the gym, with the time not said twice; each row in the list shows the time where the kg stood; the line reads vs the one before: +4 sets · −5 min; and the gym block shows the time. The best set of each machine (best 90 kg × 10) stays as it was.",
            "Workout Companion · Changed: a gym session on a day without planned strength now shows up. Before (2.16): a finished Workout Companion session only ticked a strength session that was in the plan for that same day and still to do; on a rest day or a mobility-only day it went nowhere in this app, only to Body › Gym sessions. Now: when that day has no strength session in the plan at all, the session is added by itself as an Extra workout: Strength, its minutes, its effort 1 to 10 if Workout Companion has one, counted as training, with the note From Workout Companion. It shows wherever extras show (Today, the week strip, Sessions under Done and All, Settings › Extra workouts) and adds its time to Week so far's Strength row, but only when the plan has strength that week.",
            "Workout Companion · Good to know: the rules. Today and the 13 days before. Each Workout Companion session once only, so an extra you delete does not come back. Not when that day already has a Strength extra. A day whose planned strength session is still to do is ticked as before. A day whose planned strength is already done or marked missed gets nothing. It happens on the iPhone, where Workout Companion's notes arrive. Garmin strength activities (since 2.17) still only tick planned sessions.",
            "Today · Changed: the Extra workout pill moved. Before: the small + Extra workout pill sat at the end of the Tomorrow line, so on a day without a Tomorrow line it had a different place. Now: it sits on a line of its own directly above the Week so far card, at the right, every day. Same pill, same page.",
            "Settings · Changed: the row Thursday rides is gone from Your plan. Before: a row that offered one easy ride every Thursday, from the next Monday to your race. It had already added its rides. Now: the row is removed. The 29 rides it added (Thursday 3 December to Thursday 1 July, 30 to 60 minutes, easy) stay in the plan like any other session, and their one Undo stays in Settings › Changes to the plan. Mobility and strength is now the first row there. The rides are there because on 24 November you said yes to one easy ride a week: the bike is the longest part of a 70.3 and the plan had little easy bike time.",
            "Signs · Changed: three new signs, listed in Signs in this app. A route line in a sport's colour is the route of a session of that sport. A filled chip on the Routes page means that sport's routes are shown, an outlined one hidden. A tick beside a choice on the Sleep need page marks the chosen need. The green tick keeps its one meaning: done.",
            "Unchanged: your plan (nothing in it changes by itself; the only things added are the Extra workout for a gym session, which you can delete), Mobility and Strength ticks, the morning answer, Suggestions, Garmin's numbers, Progress's other cards, your Excel copy and iCloud. Without a Garmin key the Routes card says so, and nothing breaks.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Today (the Extra workout pill), Changing the plan (Thursday rides, Mobility and strength), Extra workouts, Body (Gym sessions, Sleep debt, Sleep need), Your two neighbour apps (a gym session on a day without strength), Progress (Routes), What this app does not do and Signs in this app.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.18 (94)", date: "27 November 2026", headline: "Fifteen things for your half Ironman: a plan maker and your week shape, next week tuned, zones that keep up, a score for each session, fitter at the same pulse, a race-day forecast, course pacing, where you would gain most, a tune-up race, race week, a race report, drill cards, a swim video check and a note when a new block starts", items: [
            "Plan maker · New: Make a new plan. Before: the plan in the app (9 Sep 2026 to 8 Aug 2027) was the only one, and a new season meant building it by hand. Now: on the wide Plan page (iPad and Mac), under Ask about your plan, and on iPhone in the row of word buttons on the Sessions tab, a full-colour amber button Make a new plan. It opens the page Plan maker with four parts: The race (name, date, and Sprint, Olympic, Half (70.3) or Full), The weeks (the first day, always a Monday, set to the Monday after your plan's last session, with the line N weeks to the race), Hours a week (Lowest and Highest in half hours, easy every 3rd or 4th week, and the line that tests come about every 8 weeks) and My week shape. Make the draft builds a whole season from the rule book's blocks.",
            "Plan maker · New: the draft. Before: nothing to look at before a plan existed. Now: the Draft page has an amber head card, Draft — your plan is not changed, with the race, distance, date, weeks and hours; a season bar (Base, Build, Peak, Taper, Race week, Post-season, each its own amber shade with its weeks, like 17 wk); three tiles, Weeks, Sessions and Longest week; and the list The weeks (Week 4 · Mon 12 Oct · 5h 55m, the block, Easy week or Test week where it is one, a slim bar for the hours, and Swim 2 · Bike 2 and so on). Tap a week to see its days, each with its sport, minutes, zone and what it is for. The draft sits beside your plan: Today, Sessions and Progress show your own plan until you switch. The draft follows you between your devices. Delete draft asks first and says Your plan is not changed.",
            "Plan maker · New: Switch to this plan. Before: no way to change plan. Now: the Switch page asks From which Monday (only Mondays after today and after every done, missed, test and race session), and says in words what happens: for example From Mon 9 Aug 2027: 312 sessions added. Nothing before that day changes. It also says how many sessions of your current plan from that day on are taken out (none of them done) and how many of the draft's sessions before that day are left out. Switch from … first makes a safety copy (no copy, no switch), then changes everything in one save. Done says what was added and gives Undo the switch (it asks first; sessions you logged since stay). The switch is one entry, NEW PLAN, in Settings → Changes to the plan, with its own Undo, and shows in Safety copies as your plan just before you switched to a new plan.",
            "Plan maker · New: Ask Claude to look it over. Before: Claude only wrote words about the plan. Now: on the draft page, a button that lets Claude pick up to two small tweaks from the rules' own menu (a long ride or long run on another weekday, or Base, Build or Peak ten percent more or less) and write exactly three calm lines. The app checks every line. Use these changes remakes the draft through the rules; Keep the draft as it is leaves it. No names are sent. With Claude off, no key, no credit or no network, one grey line says so.",
            "My week shape · New: Settings → Your plan → My week shape. Before: the app had no idea which day you like for which sport. Now: a slate head card (Long ride Sat · long run Sun · rest Fri), a grid of Monday to Sunday with the words Swim, Bike, Run, Strength and Mobility (filled in the card's colour when chosen, outlined when not; the rest day allows only mobility), three menus for the long ride, the long run and the rest day, and Cancel and Save. Before you save one, the shape is learned from your plan. The Plan maker uses it for the draft.",
            "My week shape · New: Lay out my coming weeks this way. Before: moving every session to your pattern meant moving them one by one. Now: a button on the week shape page (Save first… until it is saved) opens Lay out my weeks: for example 24 sessions move in 9 weeks, the first two weeks spelled out (Tue swim → Mon), And N more weeks…, and a list of what is never moved. Take it moves them all, with one Undo (it asks first), also listed as one entry, Laid out to my week shape, in Changes to the plan; Keep my plan changes nothing. Never moved: sessions done, missed or waiting to be sent, past days, tests, races, simulations, easy, test and race weeks, and your away days.",
            "Next week, tuned · New: Today, directly under the Sunday card. From Sunday, once Sunday's sessions are logged or marked missed (or from 17:00), and through Monday until you answer, an indigo card NEXT WEEK, TUNED with the words 3 changes to next week, up to three lines like Tue run: 60 → 50 min, Wed run → easy, Sun bike: 100 → 110 min, a Why: line (for example three sessions felt hard this week) and two equal blue outlined buttons, Take it and Keep my plan. Take it writes all the changes in one save, shows Changed — Undo for the rest of the day and one Undo takes them all back. Keep my plan puts the card away. When nothing needs changing, one grey line: Next week stays as planned.",
            "Next week, tuned · Good to know: how the rule works. It looks at three signs: two or more sessions that felt harder than planned, two or more mornings you answered Bad or Tired, and Garmin's load of the last 7 days against the last 28 (more than 1.3 times). One sign: two sessions 10 percent shorter. Two signs: the interval session becomes easy and two sessions are 20 percent shorter. Three or more sessions missed: two sessions 10 percent shorter. When every session was done and felt as planned or easier, the long ride and long run can grow 10 percent. The week never grows more than 10 percent, cuts are in 5 minute steps. Never touched: tests, simulations, the race and race week, anything done, missed or past, and a session a card of yours changed in the last 7 days. No day moves. There is no card during a pause, an illness step or race week. Sleep is never read.",
            "Next week, tuned · Good to know: Claude. With Claude on, it may pick among the rule's own choices and word the Why: line (Picked by Claude from the rule book's choices). If it cannot, the usual grey Claude line says so, and the rule's own pick stands.",
            "Zones that keep up · New: Today (under the tuned card) and at the top of Settings → Your zones, a fuchsia card ZONES FROM YOUR SESSIONS — Your sessions point to stronger zones. It shows a tile for each number that moved, like THRESHOLD PULSE 160 → 164 bpm, RUN POWER none yet → 258 W or SWIM PACE 1:52 → 1:49 per 100 m (invented), with which sessions it comes from, and two equal fuchsia outlined buttons, Use the new zones and Keep mine. Before: zones changed only when you entered a test, about every 8 weeks. Now: between tests the app offers new numbers when your recent sessions show you got stronger.",
            "Zones that keep up · Good to know: how it is worked out. From the last 42 days, in each run, ride and swim the best steady stretch of laps lasting 20 to 30 minutes (pulse spread within 15 beats, power within 25 percent) gives a pulse estimate of 95 percent of that stretch's pulse; run power counts only from a stretch at 96 percent of threshold pulse or higher. In the pool the fastest lap of 400 m or more plus 3 s per 100 m. The offer shows when at least two sessions are 3 beats, 2 percent power or 2 percent pace better, and it never lowers a number. Laps that add up to more than 110 percent of the activity are ignored.",
            "Zones that keep up · New: Use the new zones enters a test result called Your sessions (notes From your sessions · run power 258 W), placed after your last test with numbers, so the tests the plan still waits for still fill in. Your zones are worked out again at once. Changed — Undo stays for the rest of the day; Undo takes the entry out on every device. Keep mine hides that offer until your sessions show clearly more again, or for 6 weeks.",
            "Run power zones · New: a gold card RUN POWER ZONES on Your zones, and a pill like Power 203–220 W beside the zone pill on a run session, with run power rows in the zone sheet. The bands are the usual run power bands: Z1 up to 80, Z2 81–88, Z3 89–95, Z4 96–105 and Z5 106 percent and above of your run threshold power. Before: a run had pulse zones only. Run power is read from Garmin with your key; it needs a recording with foot pod or watch power.",
            "Session score · New: on a done run, ride or swim, under the session's pills, one of three words in plan blue, On target, A bit hard or Too hard, with a grey line like 38 of 45 min in zone 2 (and · most of it below zone 2 when that is so). It is the share of time above the planned zone: 15 percent or less is On target, up to 35 percent A bit hard, more than that Too hard. Time below the zone never counts against you. With less than 5 minutes in zones there is no score. Before: a done session showed only your own How hard was it? number. The words describe the session, never you. Nothing to tap.",
            "Session score · Good to know: no score for a zone range like Z4–Z5, an effort-only session, a brick, strength, mobility or a rest day. Z2 + strides counts as zone 2. It needs the minutes in each pulse zone from Garmin, so it shows only with a Garmin key and a recording that matches the session. The numbers are kept on this device, by session.",
            "Session score · New: on Progress, a line in the Time in zones area, On target: 9 of 11 sessions this week (invented), counting the sessions that have a score.",
            "Fitter at the same pulse · New: on Progress, under Time in zones, a filled rose card FITTER AT THE SAME PULSE with lines like Run: 5:58 /km in Sep → 5:41 /km in Nov at the same pulse and a ride line in km/h, then a slim bar for each month with the figure beside the month. Tap it for a page with the run (pace, and power when there is enough), the ride (speed) and How it is worked out. A slower month is said plainly. Before: nothing compared your pulse with your pace over months.",
            "Fitter at the same pulse · Good to know: it uses runs and rides of 20 minutes or more whose average pulse is in your zone 2 band (from your zones, else your threshold pulse times 81 to 89 percent), the monthly middle value, from September to now. A month with fewer than 2 such sessions shows a dash and too few steady runs or rides. Run power needs at least 2 sessions with power. Without zones, one line says so.",
            "Race-day forecast · New: on the race page (Settings → Race), under the red head card, an indigo card RACE-DAY FORECAST with a range for your finish (like 5h 30m – 5h 55m, invented), the words Your likely finish time, from your fitness, the course and July weather, a tile each for Swim, T1, Bike, T2 and Run (each a range with likely), a row of small bars THE MIDDLE, WEEK BY WEEK and the grey line Narrows as the race gets closer · worked out Mon 30 Nov. A part it cannot work out says Not enough yet and what is missing. Before: the race page worked out no pace and no forecast, only the times you type.",
            "Race-day forecast · Good to know: the rules. Swim: your swim pace per 100 m plus 4 seconds, over 1900 m. Bike: the middle speed of your steady rides, adjusted for the course's climbing and for heat above 20 degrees. Run: the middle speed of your steady runs, a 4 percent fade, the course's hills and heat above 15 degrees. A ride is steady at 81 to 95 percent of threshold pulse, 60 minutes or more and not indoors; a run at the same pulse, 30 minutes or more. The range is about 12 percent wide of each part far out and about 2.5 percent in the last weeks (a little wider with fewer than 3 steady sessions), rounded outward. T1 is taken as 7m 30s and T2 as 5m, estimates. There is no run test, so the run comes from your steady runs. It is a forecast, never a target; the times you type stay yours.",
            "Course pacing · New: a full-colour button Course pacing on the race page opens a page with the bike and the run in sections: from–to kilometre, the kind of section, a note, a pulse range and a power range, with a slim bar for each section as long as its kilometres. Each kind has its colour, always beside its word: Flat blue, Rolling indigo, Climb orange, Downhill purple, Turns amber. The Jönköping course is built in (1.9 km swim; a 90 km bike with about 820 m of climbing; a 21.1 km run over two laps); another race gets a flat 70.3 default. Two grey lines say Sections are approximate and that run power appears once your steady runs carry foot pod power.",
            "Course pacing · Good to know: bike pulse is a share of your threshold pulse (flat 85–90, rolling 84–89, turns 83–88, climb 81–87, downhill under 85) and bike power a share of your FTP (flat 75–82, rolling 74–80, turns 70–78, climb 72–78, downhill up to 60). Run pulse is 82–88 in the first lap, 85–90 in the middle, 87–93 in the last, 3 points lower on a climb.",
            "Where you would gain most · New: on the race page, an orange card for each part, like Bike: 14 min behind the middle of your age group — the biggest gain (invented), with a slim bar and a grey line saying how many minutes from the fastest quarter. A Changeovers row is never named the biggest gain. A row Age group 45–49 · from Garmin has Change, a page (Cancel and Save) where you can choose another group or From Garmin. The group comes from the age Garmin holds, as a five-year group at the race year; the age itself is never kept. The comparison is with past results of this race, men's results only (the 2019, 2022 and 2023 mean, the middle and the 25th percentile). It says what is; it never says you are bad at something.",
            "Tune-up race · New: on the race page, under the countdown, Tune-up races with a red tile (TUNE-UP RACE, name, date, start, distance, place) and the button Add a tune-up race. Its page asks for Name, Date, Distance (Sprint, Olympic or Other with km), Place and Start time, with Cancel and Save, and a saved one can be taken out. After Save a card says Make room for the tune-up: Thu and Fri shorter and easy, Sat rest, Mon and Tue easy, lists each change, and offers Take it and Keep my plan. Take it makes all the changes in one save with one Undo (Changed for the tune-up — Undo). The card also shows on Today until you answer, and on its day in the week board a small red chip Tune-up race.",
            "Tune-up race · Good to know: the rules. Two and three days before, sessions become shorter (60 percent, in 5 minute steps, at least 15 minutes, never longer) and easy; the day before, sessions are taken out (mobility stays); the day after and the day after that, sessions are easy and at most 60 minutes. Never touched: done, logged, missed or waiting sessions, tests, races and days gone. A grey line says Nothing changed when the tune-up is less than 21 days from the main race, a test falls in those days, the day is past, or there is nothing to change.",
            "Race week · New: a card Race week · 5 days to go on Today and on the race page, from 7 days before the main race or a tune-up. It opens the Race week page: a card for each day, seven days before to the day before, each in its own colour, with things to tick (the tick means done, as everywhere), a RACE MORNING timeline worked back from the start (wake up 3 hours before, breakfast 2h 45m, leave 2 hours, set up the changeover 1h 45m, wetsuit 25 minutes, start), Change the start time (Cancel and Save; 08:00 is assumed until you type one) and a full-colour button Open your kit list. A sprint, an Olympic or another race has a shorter list.",
            "Race report · New: a card Race report on the race page for any past race, and on Today for 7 days afterwards. It opens a page with your total, a tile for each leg (like Bike 3h 02m · planned 3h 00m) with a slim bar and a dark mark for your plan, the distance, Garmin's own speed (swim per 100 m, bike km/h, run per km) and pulse, a part What to keep (the steadiest leg, the leg that drifted most, the changeovers; no judging) and a full-colour Share as PDF (A4). It works for a tune-up too; a plan time shows only if you typed one. The race is read from Garmin's multisport recording, once for each race day, and kept.",
            "Drill cards · New: Settings → Your plan → Drill cards, 24 cards: Swim drills (10), Strength (11) and Mobility (3). A plan-blue head card, a full-colour Swim video check button, and a grid of tiles, each its own colour. Tap one: a head naming what it is, a line drawing, steps numbered 1 to 3 and WHAT IT TRAINS. On a session's page a row like Drill cards: Catch-up, Fist opens the cards (Done or Escape closes); a swim with only the general word drill gets Drill cards: swim drills. Matching is by whole words and the longest name first, so side plank never also gives plank. Words and drawings only; nothing changes your plan.",
            "Swim video check · New: from the Drill cards page and from a swim session, Swim video check. Choose a video, and the app takes six still pictures from it. A line says Six still pictures go to Anthropic; the video stays on your device. Send to Claude · about 3 cents shows three tip cards, each its own colour with a numbered circle 1 to 3, each with a link Drill card: … Earlier checks are listed by day (tips only). The tips are shown only if there are exactly three, short, and free of words about your body, weight, health or age. The video is deleted from the app's temporary copy at once and no picture is kept. It uses your own key and counts toward the monthly Claude amount. With no key, no credit or no network, one grey line says so, for example Claude is resting: it is not switched on. Settings → Claude.",
            "Block intros · New: on the first three days of a new block (Base, Build, Peak, Taper, Race week, Post-season, or a single easy week) Today shows a green card New block: Build 1 with three short parts, WHAT IT IS FOR, WHAT WILL FEEL DIFFERENT and ONE THING TO WATCH, and a full-colour Got it. Read it again any time: tap a block's name under the season bars on the wide Plan page (the line Tap a block name to read what it is for), or the row This block: Build 1 — what it is for on a session's page, on every device. The words come from the rule book, not from Claude.",
            "Garmin · Changed: the Garmin key now also reads the minutes in each pulse zone for the session score, laps and run power for zones that keep up, steady rides and runs for the fitter card and the forecast, the age for your age group and the multisport recording of a race. All of it is only read; nothing is written to Garmin. The numbers show things and offer things, and change your plan only when you tap.",
            "Claude · Changed: one new use, the swim video check, which sends six still pictures. Claude may also look over a draft plan and pick among the rule book's choices for next week. Every answer is checked by the app, and every use counts toward your monthly amount and says plainly when it cannot be asked.",
            "Left out · Good to know: sessions on your Garmin watch. It waits until March, your choice. Today the Garmin Connect card still only lists the steps.",
            "Your plan · Good to know: nothing in your plan changes without your own tap. Every batch (next week tuned, the tune-up, the week shape, a new plan, new zones) has one Undo. Done, logged, missed and past sessions, test days and the race day are never changed.",
            "Between devices · Good to know: these follow you on iPhone, iPad and Mac through iCloud: your week shape, a plan draft and its switch, the tune-up races and their rooms, race week ticks and start times, race reports, tips from swim video checks, block intros you have read, which zone offers you took or kept, the forecast's weekly snapshot and your age group. The numbers read from Garmin stay on the device that read them.",
            "Signs · Changed: new cards and words are listed in Signs in this app. Card colours (indigo, fuchsia, gold, rose, orange, amber shades) only tell cards apart. The three score words and the course section colours always stand beside their words. The red chip Tune-up race is red because red means a race. The green tick keeps its one meaning: done.",
            "Unchanged: your plan file and the Excel copy, the morning answer, Suggestions and the Stop sign, Body, Strength and Mobility ticks, reminders and iCloud. Without a Garmin key or a Claude key, the new things that need them are simply not shown, and nothing breaks.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Today (next week tuned, zones offer, block intro, race week and race report cards), On a session's page (the score, run power pill, drill cards, swim video check and block row), Changing the plan (Plan maker and My week shape), Your zones, Your race page (forecast, pacing, where you would gain most, tune-up, race week and race report), Progress, Claude built in, Garmin parts, What this app does not do and Signs in this app.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.17 (93)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "Strength ticked from Garmin, and a strength count", items: [
            "Strength sessions · New: a strength session ticks itself when your Garmin watch recorded a strength activity. Before: a strength session ticked itself only from Workout Companion (on your iPhone). Now: when the app opens, and whenever Today appears, on any device where your Garmin key is saved (iPhone, iPad or Mac; the key is saved on each device on its own, in Settings → Garmin), the app asks Garmin for your activities of the last 14 days. A Garmin strength activity of 10 minutes or more ticks a planned strength session still to do on the same day. Nothing to tap.",
            "Time and effort · New: the activity's minutes become the session's time. No effort goes in, because Garmin does not hold your 1 to 10, so How hard was it? can still be asked.",
            "How often · Good to know: the app asks Garmin at most once every 10 minutes, and only when a strength session is still to do in those 14 days.",
            "Which days · Good to know: only today and the 13 days before; never a day ahead. On a day with two strength sessions, only the first one still to do is ticked.",
            "Left alone · Good to know: a session marked missed or waiting to be sent is never touched. A session that already had a log, even one you cleared, is never ticked from Garmin. So when you clear a Garmin tick, it stays cleared, on every device. Each Garmin activity ticks one session once, on every device.",
            "Workout Companion first · Good to know: on your iPhone a Workout Companion note ticks the session before Garmin is asked. Garmin then finds it done and leaves it.",
            "On the session · New: on Today and on the session's page, a grey line says Ticked from Garmin, on iPhone, iPad and Mac.",
            "To undo a tick: open the session and change or clear the log, the usual way.",
            "Progress · New: in the Load card, right under the Mobility line, one more grey line, for example Strength: 3 of 4 this month (invented numbers). It counts the strength sessions of your plan in this calendar month, from the 1st up to and including today: how many are done, out of how many were planned. A missed session counts as not done. Sessions later this month are not counted yet. It shows once this month has at least one planned strength session up to today, so on the 1st of a month with no strength that day it is hidden. On iPhone, iPad and Mac. A count, never a judgement.",
            "Garmin · Changed: the Garmin key was used only to show numbers (Today's morning line, Body, the laps and zones of a done session). Now it also lets a Garmin strength activity tick a planned strength session. Nothing is written to Garmin, and the numbers themselves still change no plan.",
            "Signs · Changed: the grey line Ticked from Garmin is new, and so is the grey Strength count. Both are plain notes, never a judgement. The green tick keeps its one meaning: the session is done.",
            "Unchanged: Mobility (still ticked from Magic Morning only) and the Mobility count, strength ticked from Workout Companion, your Excel copy (the Done box still says Yes), the plan, the morning answer, Suggestions, Body and iCloud. Without a Garmin key nothing changes.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Strength ticked from Garmin (new), Mobility count and Strength count, Strength ticked from Workout Companion, the Garmin parts (what the key is used for) and Signs in this app (the neighbour marks).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.16 (92)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "Strength ticked from Workout Companion", items: [
            "Strength sessions · New: a strength session ticks itself when Workout Companion noted a finished workout. Before: Today showed Done in Workouts at 07:40 · 35 min (invented) with a green Log it button, and nothing was logged until you tapped it. Now: when this app opens on your iPhone (and whenever Today appears), a planned strength session that is still to do, on a day Workout Companion noted a finished workout (a finished Sets & reps workout or a gym visit), is logged as done by itself. Nothing to tap.",
            "Time and effort · New: the workout's minutes become the session's time; if the note has no minutes, it is the planned length. If Workout Companion noted an effort from 1 to 10, it goes in too.",
            "Which days · Good to know: only today and earlier days are ticked, up to 14 days back, as long as the notes are kept. A day ahead is never ticked.",
            "Left alone · Good to know: a session you already logged, marked missed, or that waits to be sent is never touched. Each note ticks one session, once. On a day with two strength sessions only the first one still to do is ticked; a second note that day ticks the next one.",
            "On the session · New: on Today and on the session's page, a grey line says Ticked from Workout Companion. Before, the line said Done in Workouts at 07:40 · 35 min.",
            "Log it · Changed: the green Log it button now stays only as a fallback, when the tick cannot happen by itself: the note has no minutes and the session has no planned length. Then the grey line Done in Workout Companion at 07:40 · 35 min and the small green Log it show as before.",
            "To undo a tick: open the session and change or clear the log, the usual way.",
            "iPad and Mac · Changed: where a tick came from now travels with the log through iCloud. Ticked from Magic Morning (mobility, since 2.15) and Ticked from Workout Companion (strength) now show on your iPad and your Mac too. Before, they showed only on the iPhone. The ticking itself still happens on the iPhone, where the notes live. Answering How hard was it? or changing the minutes keeps the Ticked from line; clearing the log removes it. Your Excel copy is unchanged: the Done box still says Yes.",
            "Progress · New: in the Load card, right under Stretching: 4 of the last 7 mornings, one grey line, for example Mobility: 3 from Magic Morning · 1 by hand (invented numbers). It counts every logged mobility session of your plan: those ticked from Magic Morning, and those logged any other way (by hand). Missed sessions are not counted. It shows once at least one mobility session is logged, on iPhone, iPad and Mac. A count, never a judgement.",
            "Name · Changed: the neighbour app is called by its real name, Workout Companion, everywhere it was called Workouts: Done in Workout Companion, Ticked from Workout Companion, the small grey button Open Workout Companion (it was Open Workouts), and the morning line Feeling good — from Workout Companion (it was from Workouts). Magic Morning is unchanged.",
            "Signs · Changed: the grey line Ticked from Workout Companion is new, and so is the grey Mobility count. Both are plain notes, never a judgement. The green tick keeps its one meaning: the session is done.",
            "Unchanged: the morning answer, the plan, Mobility and strength, Suggestions, Body, iCloud, Garmin and your Excel file.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Your two neighbour apps (Strength ticked from Workout Companion, Mobility count, Mobility ticked from Magic Morning) and Signs in this app (the neighbour marks).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.15 (91)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "Mobility ticked from Magic Morning", items: [
            "Mobility sessions · New: a mobility session ticks itself when you stretched in Magic Morning. Before: you had to log the mobility session yourself, even when Magic Morning's routine had already had you stretching that morning. Now: when this app opens on your iPhone (and whenever Today appears), a planned mobility session that is still to do, on a day you stretched in Magic Morning, is logged as done by itself. Its time is the minutes of stretching Magic Morning noted; if the note has no minutes, it is the planned length. Nothing to tap.",
            "Which days · Good to know: only today and earlier days are ticked, up to 14 days back, as long as the notes are kept. A day ahead is never ticked. A morning without stretching ticks nothing.",
            "Left alone · Good to know: a session you already logged, marked missed, or that waits to be sent is never touched. Each stretch note ticks one session, once. A day with two mobility sessions gets only the first one ticked.",
            "On the session · New: on Today and on the session's page, a grey line says Ticked from Magic Morning. The strength line is unchanged: it still says Logged from Workouts, and a strength session still needs your tap on Log it.",
            "Where · Good to know: it works on the iPhone, where the notes live. The tick reaches your iPad and your Mac through iCloud, like any log. The grey line Stretching: 4 of the last 7 mornings (invented) on Progress is unchanged.",
            "To undo a tick: open the session and change or clear the log, the usual way. A note that ticked once does not tick again.",
            "Signs · Unchanged: no new marks. The green tick keeps its one meaning: the session is done.",
            "Unchanged: strength with Log it, the morning answer, the plan, Mobility and strength, Suggestions, Progress, Body, iCloud, Garmin and your Excel file.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Your two neighbour apps (Mobility ticked from Magic Morning), Mobility and strength and Signs in this app (the new grey line).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.14 (90)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "Mobility and strength: mobility Monday, Wednesday and Friday, strength Tuesday and Thursday", items: [
            "Settings · New: the row Mobility and strength, right under Thursday rides. Its grey line says: Mobility Mon · Wed · Fri, strength Tue · Thu, 30 min each. It shows only once the plan lives in the app, like Thursday rides.",
            "Plan · New: 30 minutes of mobility on every Monday, Wednesday and Friday, from tomorrow to the race. It is an easy session called Mobility: hips, hamstrings, calves, upper back, in the mobility colour (violet) with the mobility mark. Friday stays a rest day: mobility is easy and counts as restorative.",
            "Plan · New: strength on Tuesday and Thursday only, 30 minutes each. Before: the plan's strength sessions stood on Monday and Wednesday, with their own lengths. Now: the plan's own strength sessions move from Monday to Tuesday and from Wednesday to Thursday, keep their own exercises, and are each set to 30 minutes. A week where the plan had only one strength session gets a second one on Thursday. It is a copy of the plan's own second strength session from an earlier week, or, in a light week, the same light session again. Weeks with no strength in the plan, such as race week and the weeks after the race, get none.",
            "Plan · Good to know: race week keeps mobility only. Nothing is added after the race. A day you have already logged or marked missed is never touched. A day that already holds mobility gets no second one.",
            "The page · New: it shows, week by week, what will change, and nothing changes until you tap the one full-colour button Change N weeks (the number is the real count). Each week has a row like Week 13 · Mon 30 Nov, then Mobility Mon · Wed · Fri, then Strength Mon → Tue · Wed → Thu (or Strength Mon → Tue · + Thu), and the week's minutes before → after. Cancel closes the page without changing anything (Escape on a Mac). After the change the button goes and the top button says Done.",
            "The page · New: after the tap a green line says: Done: N mobility sessions added, N strength sessions moved, N added. Undo it all under Changes to the plan. Opening the page again once it is done says These days are already in your plan. If nothing would change it says so too. If the change fails, a red line says so and nothing is changed.",
            "Settings · New: Changes to the plan lists the whole change as one entry, CHANGED, Mobility and strength days, with how many sessions, and one Undo (it asks first). Undo takes out the mobility sessions and the added strength sessions, and puts the moved strength sessions back on their days. Anything you logged since stays.",
            "iCloud · New: you make the change on one device and it reaches your iPhone, iPad and Mac like every change to the plan. Each mobility day has one fixed name, so two devices never make two sessions on one day.",
            "Signs · Unchanged: no new marks. The arrow → still means before → after, or moves to. The plus + still means added. Mobility uses the violet and the mark it always had.",
            "Unchanged: logging, Missed, Move, Swap, Thursday rides, Suggestions, Progress, Body, iCloud, Garmin and your Excel file.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Changing the plan (Mobility and strength and its Undo) and Signs in this app (no new marks).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.13 (89)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "The gym folder now lives in your AMS Triathlon Training folder", items: [
            "Body · Changed: where the gym folder lives. Before (2.12): the folder AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin sat at the top of iCloud Drive. Now: it lives inside your own folder, iCloud Drive › Documents › 03 Home › 02 IT › 01 SW › AMS Triathlon Training › AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin, holding the Workout Companion app's file Workout Companion sessions.json. The Gym sessions card says: Your gym sessions come from the Workout Companion app. Tap Choose folder and pick AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin — it is in iCloud Drive › Documents › 03 Home › 02 IT › 01 SW › AMS Triathlon Training. Once.",
            "Settings · Changed: Settings → Garmin → Gym sessions now says where the folder is: Where: iCloud Drive › Documents › 03 Home › 02 IT › 01 SW › AMS Triathlon Training › AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin, then the button Choose the folder. Choose it again there once on each device: a choice made in 2.12 pointed at the old place.",
            "Unchanged: the Garmin Board already reads the folder at its new place (its setting was changed on your Mac); the Workout Companion app keeps writing into the moved folder; the Board's weekly reports stay in the folder AMS Garmin.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Body (Gym sessions and choosing the folder).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.12 (88)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "The gym folder has a new name: AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin", items: [
            "Body · Changed: the folder's name. Before: the gym sessions came from a folder called AMS Garmin in iCloud Drive. Now: the folder is called AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin (renamed on your Mac on 26 November; it holds only the Workout Companion app's file). The Gym sessions card says: Your gym sessions come from the Workout Companion app. Tap Choose folder and pick AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin — it is in iCloud Drive › Documents › 03 Home › 02 IT › 01 SW › AMS Triathlon Training. Once.",
            "Settings · Changed: Settings → Garmin → Gym sessions. Before: one button, Choose the AMS Garmin folder. Now: the line From the Workout Companion app, as on your Garmin Board, then In iCloud Drive: AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin, and the button Choose the folder. Once chosen, the folder's name and the newest session's day show, with a small Change button.",
            "Unchanged: the Garmin Board's weekly reports stay in the folder AMS Garmin; the Workout Companion app keeps writing into the renamed folder by itself; your plan, the other cards and the colours are as in 2.10.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Body (Gym sessions and choosing the folder).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.11 (87)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "A link to every page, so AMS Deck Mate can open Plan, Body, Progress and Settings", items: [
            "Other apps · New: a link for every page. Before: only amsworkoutsync://today opened a page (and amsworkoutsync://session/… opened one session). Now: also amsworkoutsync://plan, amsworkoutsync://sessions, amsworkoutsync://body, amsworkoutsync://progress and amsworkoutsync://settings. On an iPad and on a Mac the page is chosen in the side list. On an iPhone the tab opens. The iPhone has no Sessions tab, so amsworkoutsync://sessions opens the Plan tab there.",
            "Other apps · New: they work from anywhere. Shortcuts, Raycast, PARAGON and Safari can all use these links, not only Deck Mate.",
            "Why: AMS Deck Mate, your Stream Deck app (Mac 0.24), has a new page group Triathlon that shows whenever Triathlon is in front on your Mac. Its keys are Training today, Today, Plan, Body, Progress (each in Triathlon's own colour: Today green, Plan blue, Body pink, Progress purple), Body Battery, Sleep, Resting pulse, Stress, Steps (from the Garmin Board), the Ironman plan, Workouts, Workouts 7 days, Settings (slate) and a key back to AMS Deck. Before 2.11, the keys Plan, Body, Progress and Settings only brought Triathlon to the front; now each opens its own page.",
            "Unchanged: nothing on the screens. No new button, mark or colour. Your plan, logging, Body, Progress, Settings, Spotlight, Siri, the today link and the session links, your favourites, notes, kit and race page, and your Excel file all work as before.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Keys, Spotlight and Siri (the page links and the Deck Mate page) and Signs in this app (no new marks).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.10 (86)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "A comment with How do you feel?, and a colour of its own for every card on Body", items: [
            "Today · New: a comment with How do you feel? Before: one tap on a face and the card was gone. Now: your face is kept at once, and the card stays with Anything to add?, a field (A few words, like slept badly or sore legs) and two buttons, Save in green and Skip. On a Mac, Escape is Skip. Where: Today, under the green heading.",
            "Today · New: your comment under the morning line. Before: the morning line showed only the word you chose. Now: your comment shows under it in grey, in quotes. A tap on it opens the card again, so you can change it. It is kept in the app's diary with your answer and goes to your own iCloud, so your iPad and your Mac show it too. It is never written into your plan or your Excel file, and it leads to no advice. An answer given in Magic Morning or Workouts has no comment here.",
            "Body · Changed: a colour of its own for every card. Before: every tile and card on the Body page was the same raspberry. Now: each card's name, the marks and bars of its figures and its pale ground have the card's own colour. Sleep and Sleep debt are indigo, HRV teal, Resting pulse fuchsia, Stress amber, Steps lime, Intensity minutes blue, Training load violet, Fitness cyan, Gym sessions orange, Workouts this month pink, Weight purple, Energy gold and Water sky blue. A card's opened page uses the card's colour too.",
            "Body · Unchanged: what stays raspberry. Body Battery (the big card and the 7 days of curves), the page heading, the headings Training and Health, the range buttons and Share. Today's weekday letter stays bold green, and the normal band stays grey. No card uses the green of today and done, or the red of a warning.",
            "Body · Changed: clearer words on the Gym sessions card before you choose the folder. Before: the card asked you to choose the folder once in Settings. Now: it says Your gym sessions come from the Workout Companion app. Tap Choose folder and pick AMS Workout Companion app to Garmin — it is in iCloud Drive › Documents › 03 Home › 02 IT › 01 SW › AMS Triathlon Training. Once. The button opens the folder choice straight away. Settings → Garmin → Gym sessions still has it too.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, zones, tests, suggestions by the rule book, the Stop sign and I'm ill, your favourites, notes, kit and race page, the neighbour apps' notes and your Excel file.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Today (the morning question) and Body (the colours, and the gym card's words), and Signs in this app (Today, the morning; Body).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.9 (85)", date: "26 November 2026", headline: "Body gets the Garmin Board's missing cards: training load, fitness, gym sessions, workouts this month, sleep debt, weight, energy and water", items: [
            "Body · New: a part Training under the tiles. Before: the Body page ended with six tiles and the Share button. Now: under the tiles a small heading Training with four cards, in the look of the tiles. You picked only the cards of your Garmin Board that this page lacked, so none repeats a tile. Where: Body, under the tiles.",
            "Body · New: Training load. Before: no load on the page. Now: the last 7 days' load, the 4-week average and the ratio, a word (Recovery, Maintaining, Productive or Overreaching, the Board's own reading) and a slim raspberry scale with a darker steady stretch and a round marker. Only Overreaching is red. Tap for 12 weekly bars in the page Training load.",
            "Body · New: Fitness. Before: nothing about fitness age. Now: Garmin's fitness age against your real age, like Real age 58 · 6 years younger. VO2 max shows only when one of your workouts holds it; otherwise the card says Garmin does not share it yet. No page.",
            "Body · New: Gym sessions. Before: the gym sessions you log in AMS Workout Companion were not in this app. Now: a wide card with the latest session (kilograms, place, length, machines, sets, how it felt, the comparison with the one before), each machine's best set and the six latest sessions; a tap on a row shows that session in the card, and Back to the latest returns. No page.",
            "Body · New: choosing the gym folder. Before: nothing. Now: Settings → Garmin has a section Gym sessions with a full-colour button, Choose the folder, once. The card offers the same choice. The app only reads the folder and writes nothing to it; the choice stays on this device.",
            "Body · New: the gym block on a strength session's page. Before: a strength session's page showed its own facts only. Now: when the gym file has a session on the same day, a small GYM block shows its place, length, machines, sets and kilograms and the best sets. Other kinds of session show nothing.",
            "Body · New: Workouts this month. Before: only today's workouts were on the Body page, on the curve. Now: a wide card with the month's count, total time and distance and the newest 6 workouts, also those not in your plan, each with a sport tag; All 17 workouts opens the whole month in a sheet. A tap on a workout opens it the way a tap on the curve does (your plan's session, else your extra, else the facts plate) and changes nothing.",
            "Body · New: a part Health with four cards, shown only. Where: Body, under the Training cards.",
            "Body · New: Sleep debt. Before: the Sleep tile showed last night and a 7-night average. Now: the 7 nights against what you need, like −6h 40m beside 7 nights, seven slim bars each with a thin grey outline behind it for that night's need, and a page with each night. Naps count; 8 hours when Garmin gives no need. Shown only: sleep never leads to a suggestion, and it is never red.",
            "Body · New: Weight. Before: no weight in the app. Now: the latest weigh-in with its day, the change over 90 days, Garmin's goal when it has one, a thin line with a dot on the latest, and a page with every weigh-in.",
            "Body · New: Energy. Now: today's calories, active and resting. Garmin counts them up through the day, so the figure grows until midnight.",
            "Body · New: Water. Now: the water you logged in Garmin Connect, with a slim bar against Garmin's goal. The app does not log water.",
            "Body · Changed: empty cards. When Garmin or the file has nothing, a card keeps its name and says in one grey line what is missing and how it fills. It never shows a zero as if it were a number. Without a Garmin key each Garmin card says Add your Garmin key in Settings to fill this.",
            "Body · Changed: how the new cards read. The same key as the rest of the page, at most one read in 30 minutes for each card; pull down to read now. The gym file is read when the page opens (at most once in 5 minutes) and on pull-down. Each reading is kept on the device so the page shows at once, and an empty answer never wipes it. Nothing is written to Garmin, your plan, Dropbox or iCloud.",
            "Neighbour apps · Fixed: the today note after midnight. Before: when the app stayed open over midnight, AMS Tria Menu, AMS Deck Mate and PARAGON saw no note for the new day until the app came to the front. Now: the note is rewritten at midnight and by a check every five minutes when the day has turned. Found by the new menu bar app AMS Tria Menu.",
            "Mac · Fixed: Body numbers kept from yesterday. Before: an app started in the background on a Mac (at login, say) read no Body numbers, and the menu bar kept yesterday's Body Battery. Now: the numbers are read when the app starts, at midnight and on that five-minute check, and the first try of a new day skips the half-hour rule once. Found by AMS Tria Menu.",
            "What could only be proven on your own devices: how every new card looks on a real screen, Garmin's real answers read in the app (84 days of workouts, sleep needs, weigh-ins), the folder choice and a real gym file in iCloud Drive (on a Mac, the iPad app's read access to the folder), the gym block on a strength session, the tap on a month workout that is not in your plan, and the two fixes across a real midnight and a real Mac login. Known small things: thousands in the gym and load figures are written with a comma, and the month counts only Garmin's first 99 workouts.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, zones, tests, suggestions by the rule book, the Stop sign and I'm ill, your favourites, notes, kit and race page, the neighbour apps' notes and your Excel file. Sleep still never leads to a suggestion.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Body (the eight new cards, the Training and Health parts and the one-time gym folder choice), On a session's page (the gym block), the Garmin settings part (Gym sessions) and Signs in this app (Body).",
            "Guide · Fixed: a few wrong words. The side list on iPad and Mac has six rows (Body was missing in one place); the Garmin key words say Today and Body; the Body sample figures match the sample; the Tests card shows whenever a test has a number; Change is there only while the plan lives in the app; Apple Health also shows Connect on an iPad; and the word the shelf is gone from the guide.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.8 (84)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Forty-one things you picked: Body in more depth, reminders, away mode, a race page, notes beside a log, Garmin on a done session, and Claude on your week", items: [
            "Body · New: Body Battery · last 7 days. Before: the Body page showed today's curve and yesterday's line. Now: under the top card, seven small curves, one for each day, oldest at the left and today at the right, with the weekday letter under each (today's bold and green), then the day's highest figure and its lowest. A day without readings shows a small grey dash. Where: Body, under the top card.",
            "Body · New: Charged +44 overnight (invented). Before: the top card showed the number now. Now: beside it, how far Body Battery rose from the night's lowest reading to the morning's highest before 11:00. When it cannot be worked out, or there was no rise, nothing shows.",
            "Body · New: one calm line, like 3 of 3 in your normal range, at the top of the page. It counts where HRV, resting pulse and Body Battery on waking sit against your own normal, and names what is outside (· HRV below it). Only numbers that have a normal count. No colour and no advice, and it never leads to a suggestion.",
            "Body · New: your normal behind the bars. Before: the HRV and Resting pulse bars stood alone. Now: a grey outlined box with the word normal stands behind them: Garmin's range for HRV, and 4 percent either side of your normal for pulse. The bars are scaled to take it in.",
            "Body · New: longer views. Before: every tile showed seven days. Now: a switch under the Body Battery card, 7 days · 4 weeks · 12 weeks. The longer ones show weekly averages, one bar for each week, named by its Monday's day of the month, and the line under the switch says so. A week with no reading shows a dash, never a zero. A tile's page of numbers lists one row for each week. Garmin is asked for the days only when you pick a longer view, at most once in half an hour for each, and the days are kept on this device.",
            "Body · New: two more tiles, Steps and Intensity minutes. Before: four tiles. Now: six. Steps shows today's steps and a 7-day average; Intensity minutes shows this week's total, of the weekly goal when Garmin gives one, with the moderate and vigorous minutes (a vigorous minute counts twice, as Garmin counts it). Breathing rate and blood oxygen are not in this release.",
            "Body · New: Share. A raspberry button near the foot of Body turns the page into one picture, in the look you see now, and hands it to the share sheet. It leaves the app only if you choose a place there.",
            "Today and reminders · New: weather and daylight. Before: nothing on Today about the weather. Now: under an outdoor session of today, one grey line, like 11° · feels 7° · breezy 5 m/s · rain likely 15–16 · Light until 16:12. Outdoors means run, bike, brick, race, an open-water swim, a hike or a walk. The weather comes from Open-Meteo (the service AMS Packing uses), with your place rounded to a tenth of a degree; iOS asks Allow while using the app the first time. Settings → Weather → Weather and daylight on Today switches it off.",
            "Today and reminders · New: Week so far. A card above Tomorrow: for each sport of the plan this week, the time done of the time planned (1h 20m of 2h 30m) with a slim bar. Done is the sport's full colour, the rest pale.",
            "Today and reminders · New: The way back. Before: after an illness the rule book brought you back in steps, said in words. Now: the steps are also a small staircase on Today (while the grey ladder line shows, and in the week after) and on the I'm ill page: Rest, Two easy days, Week 1 back, Week 2 back, Back on your plan. The step you are on is filled green, steps behind carry a tick, steps ahead are pale. The words are the rule book's own.",
            "Today and reminders · New: Settings → Reminders, three notices made on your phone. Before: the app sent no notices at all. Now: an evening reminder (default 20:00) saying what tomorrow holds; a Sunday notice (default 18:00) with next week's count and hours; and a missed-session question (default 08:00) about yesterday's session that was not logged. All three are off until you switch them on, each has its own time, and Send a test now tries one.",
            "Today and reminders · New: the Sunday card. From the Sunday time until Monday 08:00, a blue card on Today, directly under today's sessions, NEXT WEEK, with the count, the hours, the phase and E or T, and a row for each session. Close puts it away until next Sunday.",
            "Today and reminders · New: missed-session choices from the notice. The morning notice Yesterday's Run was not logged has three buttons: Skip it, Move to today (left out when the app cannot change the plan or the rule book has a remark) and It is done (opens the session's log form). The buttons open the app first, so the plan is loaded; if anything changed meanwhile, the app opens on that session and does nothing. Nothing is sent while the Stop sign or I'm ill is on.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Away. Before: no way to tell the app about a trip. Now: Settings → Your plan → Away: from, until, and four switches for what you have there (Pool, Bike, Gym, Open water). Sessions inside the period that need what you lack carry a grey chip (No pool while away) and Today gets one grey line. A new rule book trigger, AW, can offer a swap with a later easy session, a move to the first day after you are back, or rest. It never adds or lengthens anything, and every rule of the rule book still judges each choice. It follows you between devices.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: No-gym version. On a strength session, a button that shows a circuit of body weight, a number of rounds of 8 moves, with a warm-up, a rest and a cool-down, in about the planned time. Text only; it changes nothing. While you are away without a gym, it is filled and says First choice while away without a gym.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: favourite sessions. Before: a new session was typed from the start. Now: Save as favourite on a session's page keeps its sport, title, purpose, length and zone (up to 40); the New session page has a block Your favourites, and a tap fills the form. Settings → Your plan → Favourite sessions lists them, with Rename, Remove and drag to arrange by a handle of three lines. They follow you between devices.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: repeat a session. Before: one session at a time. Now: the New session page has Repeat, Every week until a date, and lists every day it will add and what it leaves out (a day with the same session, race week, outside the plan). An existing session has Repeat…. In Changes to the plan the repeats are one entry with one Undo.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Search. Before: the Sessions page had four filters only. Now: a field, Search sessions, finds sessions and extras by any words in the title, notes, sport and date, grouped To come, Done and Missed. On an iPad or Mac, Command and F goes to it.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Print. A Print button in the row of small word buttons under the Sessions heading (and on the wide Plan page): this week, next week or this month on one A4 page, as a PDF or to a printer.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: the pool card. On a swim, a button Pool card shows the set in large type, one step at a time, with Back and Next, and keeps the screen awake. What it cannot read stays as its own row.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Why this session. Under the title of every session except a rest day, and on today's card, one grey line, Why: …, with what that kind of session is for.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Race page. Before: the race was a flag and a countdown on Progress. Now: Settings → Race and kit → Race (and from Progress and the Plan numbers) opens a page: a red head card with the countdown (red is only the head card, the headings and the tile names; the buttons are blue); Your plan for the day (times you type for swim, T1, bike, T2 and run, and the finish they add up to, with no pace or forecast); a fuel plan with grams per hour; and a kit checklist (starting with 21 items) you can change and drag. It follows you between devices.",
            "Plan and sessions · New: Shoes and bikes. Settings → Race and kit → Shoes and bikes counts kilometres on each pair of shoes and each bike from your logged runs and rides, against a limit you set, with Use from today, Put aside, Retire and Remove. Past the limit one grey line, no red. It follows you between devices.",
            "After a session · New: From your watch. Before: a done session showed what you typed. Now, with a Garmin key: the route as a line and the pulse curve (Average 138 · Highest 156 beats, invented), after your notes and before the photographs. Not for a pool or an indoor session.",
            "After a session · New: Laps. A table of Lap, Distance, Time and Pulse (and km/h and Watts when Garmin gives them); the first twelve laps, then Show all 27 laps.",
            "After a session · New: Last time. A card setting this session beside the last time you did the same kind (the same sport and title): length, distance, average pulse and how hard, each as now ← last time. It needs no Garmin key.",
            "After a session · New: Stomach OK?. On sessions of 90 minutes or longer, Fine, So-so or Upset and a line of what you ate and drank. Fuel notes lists every answer with a tally.",
            "After a session · New: Niggle?. A place, a side and a line of your words, on the log form and on a done session. A note for yourself, not advice.",
            "After a session · New: brick log. On a brick session, three boxes, Bike time, Change-over and Run time, and an offer to use their sum as the length.",
            "After a session · New: open-water notes. On a swim, a switch Open water, then wetsuit, water temperature and a line on sighting and conditions.",
            "Progress · New: Month in review. A purple card for the month before today, from the 1st: hours, sessions, plan followed (the Plan page's figure), the longest session, hours per sport, how you felt by word, and a closing line. Earlier months lists every finished month.",
            "Progress · New: Your bests. Longest ride, run and swim, your biggest week and your longest row of weeks. The session tiles open that session.",
            "Progress · New: Tests. Threshold pulse, bike power and swim pace across all your tests, as a newest value and a small chart with one dot for each test.",
            "Progress · New: Time in zones. This week's minutes in each pulse zone, Z1 to Z5, from Garmin, with last week in words and, when the sessions name zones, a grey line of what the plan asked for.",
            "Progress · New: Steady weeks. How many weeks in a row followed the plan (90 percent or more of the Plan page's figure), with twelve small squares. This week adds one but never breaks the row. No prize.",
            "Progress · New: Niggles. Each place you noted, with how often and since when, then every note by date. A notebook, not a diagnosis.",
            "Progress · New: Report as PDF. A button on the month card makes an A4 PDF of the month (facts, hours per sport, week by week, tests, zones, your mornings and a list of sessions), to send to a coach or a doctor.",
            "Suggestions and Claude · New: Your week with Claude. Before: Claude only picked among the rule book's choices. Now, from Sunday 17:00 to the end of Monday, a card on Today with the button Write my week: five short lines about the week and one question. The week's numbers and your morning words are sent, with no names, notes or titles; the answer is checked before it is shown. One for each week, the last twelve kept on this device under Settings → Claude. It counts toward the 5 US dollars a month.",
            "Suggestions and Claude · New: Ask about your plan. A small button in the row of word buttons under the Sessions heading, on the wide Plan page and in Settings → Claude opens a page where you write a question in your own words, like Why is Thursday's ride only 45 minutes?. The plan's days and the rule book's limits in words are sent, with no titles, notes or Garmin and Health numbers. A question about illness or pain is answered by the app itself, with nothing sent. The last five are kept on this device.",
            "Suggestions and Claude · Changed: the Claude page now says what each answer was for in its log, and the paragraph on Settings → Claude covers the two new uses. The key, the cost count and the cap are as before.",
            "Mac, iPad, Spotlight and Siri · New: keys. Before: Command 1 to 6 and Escape. Now: also Command N (a new session), the arrows for the week or month, Command T (today), Space on an open session (Done as planned) and Command F (search), with the word Keys at the foot of the side list showing them all (also ? and Command /).",
            "Mac, iPad, Spotlight and Siri · New: Spotlight. The sessions of the next 14 days still to do and the last 14 days done can be found from Spotlight, like Tue 1 Dec · Swim · 40 min, and a tap opens the session.",
            "Mac, iPad, Spotlight and Siri · New: Siri and Shortcuts. What is my session today in Triathlon; Log today's run as done in Triathlon (it changes nothing when there are two sessions, none, or it is done already); How is my week in Triathlon.",
            "Behind the scenes · New: an extra file that travels beside the plan. Your favourites, your away period, the notes beside a log, your shoes and bikes and your race page are kept in one small extra file in your own iCloud, met after the plan, so it can never hold the plan back. A thing that is not readable is put aside and the app opens as usual. It is not in the safety copies.",
            "Behind the scenes · Changed: what stays on one device. The reminders and their times, the weather switch, your weeks with Claude and your last questions, Garmin's answers for a session and the days kept for the longer Body views are kept on each device by itself.",
            "Behind the scenes · Changed: Settings. New rows: Reminders, Weather (under Reminders), Away, Favourite sessions, Race and kit (Race, Shoes and bikes). Settings → Claude has a row Ask about your plan and a list Your weeks with Claude.",
            "Behind the scenes · Changed: Settings → Weather sits under Reminders; its line says that a rounded place, about 10 km wide, is sent.",
            "Safer · Fixed: Space on an open session. Before: a space typed in the Why? box of the Missed question, or with a sheet open over the page, could log the session as done. Now: Space logs Done only when no box, question or sheet of the page is open.",
            "Safer · Fixed: Undo of a repeat. Before: the group Undo also took out sessions you had logged since. Now: logged, missed and waiting sessions stay, and the question says so. A second tap on Save no longer adds the session twice.",
            "Safer · Fixed: notes beside a log. Before: notes were kept after the log, so a failure was silent and a double tap on Save could queue the log twice. Now: the notes are kept first; if they cannot be kept, nothing is logged and the app says Not saved. Notes alone never log the session, and a second tap does nothing. Every change to a favourite, away period, gear or race item that cannot be kept now says Not saved out loud.",
            "Safer · Fixed: the extra file on a locked device. Before: that file that could not be read for a moment could be put aside, and your favourites, race list and gear would vanish from the screen. Now: a read that fails blocks writing and is tried again; only a file that cannot be understood is put aside.",
            "Safer · Fixed: Siri's log phrase needs the phone unlocked. Before: it could start the plan on a locked phone. Now: all three phrases need an unlocked phone.",
            "Safer · Fixed: an away card in the suggestions' notes is written under its own key, with its place in the list, so an older version of the app skips it and can still read the rest. Also: a damaged Garmin recording or an absurd number can no longer crash the reader, and a cancelled re-planning of notices no longer adds notices.",
            "Neighbour apps · New: Settings has a heading Your two neighbour apps, above Reminders, with a row Today's session is shared. Before: the app told no other app about your day. Now: it writes a small today note for AMS Deck Mate and PARAGON: today's sessions (sport, title, length and whether each is done, missed, to do or a rest day), tomorrow's first session and the week's time done of planned. No health numbers, nothing leaves your device, and nothing else is shared. It also accepts one link that logs today's session as planned, exactly as the Done button does, only when it is today's, to do, has a length, logging is allowed on that device and the plan is loaded; otherwise the link only opens the session. Deck Mate's key and PARAGON's line themselves are not in this version yet: this is only the side of this app that they will read.",
            "What could only be proven on your own devices: the Siri phrases, Spotlight, the hardware keys on an iPad or Mac, real notices and their three buttons, the question about your place and the live weather, Garmin's real answers for routes, laps, zones, steps and the Body Battery week, dragging with a real finger and pointer (favourites, fuel rows, kit), two devices meeting through iCloud, printing and the PDFs, and Claude's real answers (how often a written week passes the app's check). Also unproven: the today note read by Deck Mate and PARAGON (they do not read it yet) and the Mac file's place. Everything else was tested by the app's own checks; if any of these misbehaves, say what you saw.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, zones, tests, suggestions by the rule book (apart from Away), the Stop sign and I'm ill, the neighbour apps' notes, the Training calendar and your Excel file. Sleep still never leads to a suggestion.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: What this app is (unchanged tabs); Notes that travel beside the plan, Reminders and Notes beside a log, The pool card, From your watch on a done session, Favourite sessions and repeating, Search and print, Keys, Spotlight and Siri, Away, Your race page and Shoes and bikes are new parts; Today, On a session's page, Body, Claude built in, Progress, Suggestions by the rule book and What this app does not do changed; and Signs in this app has five new paragraphs and a longer Body."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.7 (83)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Tap a workout on the Body page, and yesterday's Body Battery beside today's", items: [
            "New: tap a workout on the Body page. Before: the workouts on the Body Battery curve only showed, and a tap did nothing. Now: tap a workout (its words, its bar, or anywhere in the column under them; the tap area is at least 44 points wide) and a page opens.",
            "New: which page opens, in this order. First, if your plan has a session of that sport on that day, that session's page opens, right there on the Body page, with the back arrow at the top left leading back to Body. With two workouts of one sport and two sessions of that sport on the day, the first workout opens the first session and the second the second. Second, if there is no such session but you have an extra of that kind on that day (a Walk extra for a walk from the watch), that extra's page opens, the same page as when you tap an extra on Today. Third, a looser match: a walk or hike opens that day's run session; a swim, ride or run opens that day's Brick or Race session. Fourth, if nothing matches, a small plate opens with the workout's own facts.",
            "New: the facts plate. Before: nothing opened. Now: its title is the workout's name from Garmin, like Morning run, then Started 06:45 · Lasted 1h 00m · Body Battery −17 (or no cost from Garmin when Garmin gives none), one grey line, Not in your plan and not among your extras for this day., and Done at the top right (Escape on a Mac). The numbers here are invented.",
            "New: how a workout's sport is told. Garmin's own sport name decides: swim, bike, run, strength, rowing, mobility (yoga, pilates, stretching) or walk (walk or hike). Anything else is other and goes to the facts plate. Only the same calendar day counts, and a rest day never matches.",
            "New: yesterday's line. Before: the Body Battery card showed today only. Now: yesterday's Body Battery is drawn too, as a thin line across the whole 24 hours, behind today's curve, with no fill under it. Today's curve is unchanged: the thick white line with a soft fill, and the white dot is still now.",
            "New: yesterday's line is named on the card. At the top right stands a short piece of the same line and the word yesterday.",
            "New: the look of yesterday's line is a thin dark line, a deep plum, darker than the card. You picked it from a picture with three looks; the other two were a thin white line and white dashes.",
            "Good to know: why yesterday's line is not pale and not dotted. In this app pale already means still to do, and dotted already means an extra outside the plan, so yesterday's line is neither.",
            "Good to know: a day without yesterday's readings (the watch was not worn, or it is your first day) simply shows no second line and no word yesterday.",
            "Changed: the foot of the Body page. Before: Tap a tile for its 7 days in numbers. Now: Tap a workout or a tile for more. The second line is unchanged: From your Garmin watch · shown only, it changes no plan.",
            "Changed: what is read from Garmin. Before: today's numbers only. Now: one more small read, yesterday's curve. Yesterday cannot change any more, so it is read once a day and then kept on the device. The rule is the same as before: at most one read in half an hour, and pulling down reads now. Nothing is written to Garmin.",
            "Good to know: a tap on a workout only opens a page. It logs nothing, writes nothing and changes no plan. The Body page is still shown only.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, Progress, zones, tests, suggestions, Claude, iCloud, the Training calendar, photographs, the four tiles and the neighbour apps' notes. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Body; Signs in this app (Body)."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.6 (82)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "A page for your body: Body Battery, sleep, HRV, resting pulse and stress from Garmin", items: [
            "New: the Body page. Your Garmin watch's numbers have a page of their own, like the Garmin Board on the Mac. On an iPhone it is a fifth tab in the middle of the bar. Before: Today · Sessions · Progress · Settings, four tabs. Now: Today · Sessions · Body · Progress · Settings, five. On an iPad and a Mac it is its own row in the side list. Before: Today · Plan · Sessions · Progress · Settings. Now: Today · Plan · Sessions · Body · Progress · Settings. On a Mac, Command and 1 to 6 choose a row (before 1 to 5). Its mark is a heart with a pulse line. Tapping the Body tab again does nothing special.",
            "New: Body has its own colour, raspberry, a deep pink. It is used for the page's heading, its top card and its tab, and nowhere else in the app.",
            "New: the top card, Body Battery. It is filled with raspberry, with white words. It shows the number now, with the word now, like 41, and beside it Highest today 82 and, when there were workouts, 2 workouts took 27 (the points the day's workouts cost; only workouts whose cost Garmin gives are counted). Under it: the curve from midnight to now, ending at a white dot, with the rest of the day left empty; an hour scale 00 · 06 · 12 · 18 · 24; and each of today's workouts as a short solid white bar above the curve, as long as the workout lasted, with its words above it and a thin white line down from each end (Run −18, Swim −9). A workout whose cost Garmin does not give shows its name only. The numbers here are invented.",
            "New: four tiles, Sleep, HRV, Resting pulse and Stress. Each has its name in small capitals, the figure right beside its unit, one grey line, and seven slim bars for the last seven days with the weekday letters under them. Sleep: last night's time, like 6h 10m, and 7-night average 5h 50m. HRV: last night's value, like 48 ms, and your normal 42–55; while Garmin has no normal range yet, the line reads still learning your normal (Garmin needs about three weeks of nights). Resting pulse: today's, like 52 beats, and your normal 51. Stress: today's average, like 31 average, and highest today 74.",
            "New: a day without a reading shows a small grey dash – where its bar would be, never a zero. All seven bars are the same full raspberry. Today's bar is the last one, and its weekday letter is bold and green.",
            "New: tap a tile for a small page with that instrument's seven days in numbers, newest first. Its title is like Sleep · last 7 days; the first row reads Today (for Sleep and HRV, Last night); a day without data reads no reading. Done closes it; on a Mac Escape closes it. The page's foot says so: Tap a tile for its 7 days in numbers.",
            "New: where the numbers come from. Straight from Garmin, with the personal key saved in Settings → Garmin, the same key the morning numbers on Today use. The page reads Garmin when it opens, at most once in 30 minutes; pull down to read now. The top line says the day and when the numbers were read, like Wed 25 Nov · read 17:31. The last reading is kept on the device, so the page shows at once. Nothing leaves the device except the question to Garmin, and nothing is written to Garmin.",
            "New: shown only. The Body page changes no plan and makes no suggestion, and sleep never leads to a suggestion. The foot says: From your Garmin watch · shown only, it changes no plan.",
            "New: without a Garmin key the page says Connect your Garmin key to see your body's numbers here, with a full-colour button, Open Garmin settings, that opens the Garmin settings page right there on the Body page (the same page as Settings → Garmin). With a key but no numbers yet it says No numbers from Garmin yet. Wear the watch, sync it in Garmin Connect, then pull down here.",
            "Good to know: between midnight and about four in the morning the curve can be empty, because the day has only begun. Sleep and HRV then still show the night before.",
            "Good to know: the AMS Garmin Board on the Mac keeps running. The Body page does not replace it; it shows several of its instruments in this app's own look.",
            "Changed: the key in Settings → Garmin now feeds two places, the morning line on Today and the Body page. Before: Today only. Nothing to set up again.",
            "Fixed, behind the scenes: GitHub's test run now gives up on a test machine that never starts after 20 minutes, instead of hanging for 30.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, Progress, zones, tests, suggestions, Claude, iCloud, the Training calendar, photographs and the neighbour apps' notes. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: What this app is (five tabs); On iPad and Mac (the side list and Command 1 to 6); Body is a new part; Morning numbers from Garmin (one key, two places); What this app does not do; and Signs in this app (The five tabs, On iPad and Mac, and a new part, Body).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.5 (81)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Your data kept safer, one number for one thing, a tidier look on iPhone, iPad and Mac", items: [
            "Fixed, kept safe: the Thursday rides. Before: adding the Thursday rides on two devices before iCloud had carried the first set over gave two rides on each Thursday. Now: each ride has one fixed name for its week, the same on every device, so the two plans join into one ride per Thursday. Adding the rides to a plan that already holds them adds nothing.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: suggestions and a plan that changed under them. Before: right after a change from another device arrived, a suggestion (and Claude's answer to it) could still be worked out from the old plan, and Take it could write over that change. Now: whenever the plan has changed, the suggestion is worked out again from the new plan, so Take it cannot overwrite a change from another device.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: Go back to Excel. Before: it was offered as soon as the iPhone knew of no other device, even though an iPad or Mac that uses the plan might not have been heard from yet. Now: it is offered only once iCloud has checked whether your iPad or Mac uses the plan too. Until then a grey line in Settings → Your plan says: Going back to Excel is offered once iCloud has checked whether your iPad or Mac uses this plan too. Also new: if the plan changed while the spreadsheet was being prepared, the Excel file is not written, and the app says The plan changed while it was being written back. Nothing was switched; try again.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: a morning answer taken over from Magic Morning. Before: it was stamped with the moment the app took it over, so it could replace an answer you gave later in this app on another device. Now: it keeps the time it was given in Magic Morning, so a later answer given here is not replaced.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: when the plan file will not open. Before: the app took the start-of-day safety copy, even when a later copy of the same day existed. Now: it takes the newest safety copy, by the time it was made.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: an iPad or Mac that still shows the old Excel plan. Before: you could log into that old plan there, and the entry was lost when the device took iCloud's plan a moment later; Today offered Connect Dropbox. Now: such a device cannot log into it, and Today shows, in grey, The plan is on its way from iCloud. Only the iPhone logs into Excel.",
            "Fixed, kept safe: an entry still waiting from the Excel days. Before: it could be written into another session that now carries the same row name. Now: it is written only into the session it was made for, matched by its sport and its day or its wording; if that session is gone, the entry waits with its reason. It is marked done at the time you logged it, not at the time it was written.",
            "Changed, one number for one thing: how sessions are counted. Before: Safety copies (310 sessions · 64 done), the iCloud page (N sessions, M done) and the line Plan from your iPhone · N sessions counted rest days as sessions, so they showed a bigger number than the Sessions tab and Settings → Your plan. Now: all of them count sessions without rest days, the same number everywhere. The numbers here are invented.",
            "Changed on the Plan page, iPad and Mac: Week, By sport. Before: a row read 45m of 1h 55m, and a sport with nothing done read 40m. Now: 45m done of 1h 55m, and 40m planned. Plan followed. Before: 3 of 3 sessions. Now: 3 of 3 sessions due so far, and, when a session was done before its day, a grey line, 1 more done ahead of its day. It counts in the hours done, not in Plan followed, so the two agree. Load. Before: titled Load, last 12 weeks, with This week 120 · usual 110. Now: Load · last 12 weeks, up to today, whatever week you chose, with This week so far and usual week, the line Load = minutes × how hard (1–10), and numbers written as on Progress (1,671, with a real minus sign).",
            "Changed on Progress: words that were confusing. The race card said done of 84; now it says done so far, of 84 in the plan. So far said 82 of 84 sessions behind you were completed; now it says Of the 84 sessions due up to yesterday, 82 were done (invented numbers), and the figure under it reads done instead of completed. Consistency said current run and longest run, which sounded like the sport Run; now it says in a row now and most in a row.",
            "Changed everywhere: lengths of time are written one way. Before: 35 min beside 42m, 0s, 7 h 20 for Garmin sleep, 66h with no minutes. Now: 1h 10m, 45m, 66h 08m, and Garmin sleep reads 7h 20m. A length of nothing reads 0m, never 0s. A length never breaks over two lines.",
            "Fixed on Today (iPhone): Answered in Magic Morning — change it there. was drawn on top of the Garmin numbers line when both showed. Now each has its own line. When the Garmin numbers do not fit one line, they break between two figures, never after a stray dot.",
            "Changed on a to-do session's page: Done · 1h 10m is a full green button. Before: it was as pale as the three buttons beside it (Log details, Missed, Move). Save on the Garmin page and on the Claude page is full colour too, and on the log form Use (for a workout from Apple Health) is an outlined button, so that only Save is full colour.",
            "Changed: figures stand beside their names. The zone sheet's rows, the Progress cards Which sport runs behind and Where the hours went, the This week card on Today (the hours now stand under the title, on the left) and the date beside the version in What's new. Before: the figure sat at the far right edge.",
            "Changed: every page under Settings has the same small centred title. Before: Garmin, Claude and The plan moves in had a large one. Also: Save it on a new extra workout is Save, and the Garmin morning plate has Done at the top right.",
            "Changed: How this works has real headings. Each part's name is larger, bold and green, so the long page can be looked through.",
            "Changed at night: every full-colour main button uses the same deeper green (Enter a test result was a bright mint). Still-to-do bars on Today's week strip, and still-to-do squares on Year, are brighter at night, so the sports can be told apart. By day nothing changes; the sign is the same.",
            "Changed, smaller: the zone sheet is as tall as what it says. In Enter a test result the boxes line up in one column. The average heart rate box shows a grey example, e.g. 135, like the other boxes. A rest day in Sessions no longer shows an empty pill with a dash. Rest / not a plan sport has its own row in Colours and shapes. The iCloud page's Your devices box is as wide as the cards around it.",
            "Changed: a first run with no plan. Before: Today showed 0s planned and an empty week card. Now: one grey line, No plan yet — Settings → Your plan brings it in.",
            "Changed: today's line in the road on Progress is green (before: dark), because today is green everywhere. Escape is Cancel on the Move page too, on a Mac.",
            "Changed, words: Progress's foot line, the Missed or moved card and Your zones no longer speak of the workbook once the plan lives in the app. Photos says On this device only on an iPad or Mac (before: On this phone only). Settings on an iPad or Mac with iCloud off says Lives in this app — iCloud is off (before: Lives in this app and in iCloud, right under iCloud is off). The iCloud page shows no Sync now button while iCloud is off.",
            "Changed on the Plan page, iPad and Mac: Month. Before: when the full titles did not fit the window's height, landscape cut off today's week and showed less than portrait, and an extra's name was cut (Stre…). Now: when full titles would not fit, the chips say the sport, the month opens with today's week in view, and an extra's name has the chip's whole width.",
            "Changed on the Plan page, iPad and Mac: Week. Before: an iPad held upright showed four days and a sideways swipe. Now: two rows, Mon–Thu over Fri–Sun, all seven days in view. The week's heading always sits on its own line under the switch and buttons. Monday and the 1st of a month carry the month (Mon 22 Mar). A range like 95–105 rpm never breaks in the middle.",
            "Changed on the Plan page, iPad and Mac: Year. Every month card has its hours on the second line, under its name, and all cards are the same height. The Phases stand in two columns (before: one long column).",
            "Fixed on the season bars: the green Today line no longer runs through the letter E or T of today's week.",
            "Fixed: VoiceOver says Done on the green tick again. It was lost in 2.4, when the drawn marks moved to the shared icon library.",
            "Fixed: the guide itself. Wrong or out-of-date sentences in How this works, in What's new 2.2 and in the specification were corrected (the old Season page, Excel described as the plan's normal home, the order of things on Today, and more).",
            "How this works changed in these parts: What this app is; Where the plan lives (Go back to Excel); The same plan on all your devices; Today; Logging a session; The Sessions tab; On iPad and Mac (the Plan page, all four views and the numbers); Changing the plan (Thursday rides); Suggestions by the rule book; How your plan is kept safe (Safety copies); Photographs; Morning numbers from Garmin; Claude built in; Your two neighbour apps; Progress; Your zones; and Signs in this app (Today, the week card and the top; Progress tab; On iPad and Mac, the Plan page; colours of the sports).",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.4.2 (80)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Not well? is quiet at the foot of Today", items: [
            "Changed: where the small button Not well? sits on Today. Before: it was a small pill in Today's green near the top of the screen, at the right end of the title How do you feel? while the morning question was open, and on a row of its own just under the morning line afterwards. You said it was a very prominent place and did not feel positive. Now: it is one small grey pill at the very foot of Today, in the middle, under everything else, even under tomorrow. It is no longer beside or under the morning question. It still shows on Today only once the plan lives in the app.",
            "Changed: its colour on a session's page. Before: the pill at the foot of a session's page was green, like Today. Now: it is grey there too, and it stays at the foot as before.",
            "Unchanged: what it opens. The same small plate with two rows, Stop sign and I'm ill, with the same words and the same pages. Nothing else changed: no plan, no rule, no other screen.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Today; Stop sign, I'm ill and Something hurts; and Signs in this app (Today, the morning; Suggestions). The pill is described as a button with its words, not as a new meaning of grey.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.4.1 (79)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "The Mac takes the plan from iCloud; easy and test weeks carry a letter", items: [
            "Fixed: a Mac or iPad that still held a link to the old Excel file. Before: such a device went on showing that old Excel file, which nobody writes any more since the plan moved into the app. Today offered Connect Dropbox at the top right, and the side list still said Same on all devices, which was not true for the plan. This happened on your Mac, from a link made in September. Now: as soon as the plan from the app is in iCloud, an iPad or Mac takes that plan by itself, the same way a new device does. Connect Dropbox no longer shows there, and what you log on your iPhone shows on the Mac. Nothing is lost: the old Excel copy on the Mac is left where it is. Your iPhone is not changed by this; an iPhone still on Excel is asked on its move-in page, as before.",
            "Changed on iPad and Mac: an easy week on the season bars. Before: an easy week was a pale bar, and the word Easy stood above it only where the bar was wide enough. Now: every bar has its phase's full colour, and an easy week carries a small letter E above its bar. Where the bars are wide enough, in a wide window, the whole word Easy stands there instead of the letter.",
            "Changed: a test week. Before: the word Test stood above a test week only where there was room, and a narrow bar showed nothing. Now: a test week always shows on the bars, with a small letter T, or the whole word Test on wide bars.",
            "Changed: the line under the bars. Before: Pale = easy week · Tap a bar to see its week. Now, when letters are shown: E = easy week · T = test week · Tap a bar to see its week, naming only the letters that occur in your plan. When the whole words are shown it says just Tap a bar to see its week.",
            "Changed: the outline round the week you chose now goes round its letter too.",
            "Why: pale means still to do on the Year page and in By sport, and a pale bar meant an easy week on the season bars, so one sign had two meanings. Now pale means one thing in the whole app: still to do. An easy week is still a shorter bar by itself, because less is planned.",
            "Stays the same: the iPhone has no season bars and looks as before. Bar heights, phase colours, the outline, the Today line, the race flag, and tapping a bar to open its week do not change. No figure and nothing in your plan changes.",
            "How this works changed in these parts: Plan, the season bars; Season (in the words about the Plan page); and Signs in this app, On iPad and Mac, the Plan page.",
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.4 (78)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Claude tells you when it cannot choose, one morning answer everywhere, signs made clearer", items: [
            "New: Claude tells you when it cannot choose. Before: when Anthropic refused (the key had ended, or there was no credit), the app quietly used the rule book's pick, and only a line in the log under Settings → Claude said so. Now: while the trouble lasts, Settings → Claude shows one line under Key saved, and the suggestion card on Today shows one grey line under the reason. It clears by itself at the next answer that works, or when you type a new key, and it stays when you close the app.",
            "New: three cases, in these words. Key no longer accepted: Anthropic no longer accepts this key. It may have ended or been removed. Until you type a new one, the rule book chooses alone. (On the card: Claude could not choose: Anthropic no longer accepts your key. Settings → Claude.) No credit: Your Anthropic account has no credit left. Until you add credit at Anthropic, the rule book chooses alone. (On the card: Claude could not choose: your Anthropic account has no credit left. Settings → Claude.) The month's cap reached: This month's 5 US dollars are used. Claude chooses again next month. Until then the rule book chooses alone. (On the card: Claude could not choose: this month's 5 US dollars are used.)",
            "New: the row Settings → Claude then reads On, but not choosing · followed by key no longer accepted, no credit left at Anthropic, or this month's 5 US dollars are used.",
            "Good to know: a short hiccup, like no network or Anthropic being busy, shows nothing on the card. It is still one line in the log, as before. The suggestion itself always appears and works: only who picks changes. Nothing is ever bought by the app.",
            "Fixed: a morning answer taken over from AMS Magic Morning Routine now says so on every device. Before: only the iPhone that took it over showed Feeling good — from Magic Morning and kept it unchangeable; an iPad or Mac that got the answer through iCloud showed it as its own and let you change it. Now: the answer carries where it came from, so your iPad and Mac show the same line and Answered in Magic Morning — change it there. An answer you give in this app removes that note. An older version of the app ignores it.",
            "Fixed: on the Year page today's day is outlined in green, as today is everywhere else (before: a dark outline). The key under the months shows the green outline beside Today.",
            "Fixed: Waiting to sync, and the waiting headline on a session's page, are grey (before: green, which means done). Green now means done and nothing else.",
            "Changed: the button Send it now in the red warning at the top of Today is green (before: red). Red stays for the warning's frame and for things that take something away.",
            "Changed: buttons that were only a mark now carry a word. The share mark says Send, on a session's page and on photographs. The flag on Progress says The race. In Move, +1 now reads +1 day. The small mark on an extra now reads Counts as training.",
            "Fixed: on Sessions, the numbers no longer count rest days. Before, Upcoming and All counted every rest day still to come as if it were a session, and the bar did too. Now Upcoming holds only sessions to do, All is Done plus Missed plus Upcoming, and the bar shows the same three. Your Upcoming and All numbers are therefore smaller than yesterday, by the number of rest days ahead. The lists still show the rest days.",
            "Fixed: a race day's badge shows the flag (before: the general other mark), so the flag means the race everywhere.",
            "Changed: all the app's hand-drawn marks now come from the central AMS icon library that every AMS app shares. Nothing looks different.",
            "Unchanged: your plan, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, Progress, zones, tests, iCloud, Garmin, the Training calendar, photographs and the neighbour apps' notes. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "New in How this works: Claude built in says what happens when Claude cannot choose; Your two neighbour apps and Today, the morning say the answer's origin is the same on every device; The Sessions tab, On iPad and Mac (Year), Missed, Move, Swap, Extra workouts, How your plan is kept safe, Progress and Sending a session say what changed. Signs in this app has the new grey line on a card, the green outline on Year, the grey waiting words, the green Send it now, the flag on a race day, and the words beside marks."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.3 (77)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Suggestions by the rule book, Claude built in, your two neighbour apps", items: [
            "New: suggestions by the rule book. The app can now suggest a change to your plan. It follows a fixed rule book, written from your own training guide and the same every time. It is not a coach and not a doctor, and says so on every card: Training suggestion — not medical advice. The app suggests, you decide: nothing in your plan changes until you tap Take it.",
            "New: the card. On Today, under the morning question, a card has one line with the change, one grey line with the reason (starting Why:), and two buttons of the same size and the same blue outline: Take it and Keep my plan. Keep my plan weighs exactly as much as Take it. Other choice shows at most two more ways to answer. After Take it, the card's place says Changed — Undo until the end of the day. A card you leave alone closes at the end of the day of its first session, as Keep my plan.",
            "New: what a card is about. Tired signs (two poor mornings in a row, or two sessions that felt much harder than planned), a key session you missed in a gap of two or three days, coming back after four days or more without training, a long ride or run planned too far beyond your recent longest, a big week last week, and, if you tell it, something that hurts. Each can only make things smaller, easier, later or a rest. It can never add a session, make anything longer or harder, make up what you missed, use a Friday, make two hard days in a row, touch a test, a race simulation, the race or race week.",
            "New: it stays calm. One card a day at most, two in any seven days, never two open at once, none in race week. After Keep my plan the same subject is left alone for a while. A session a card changed is left alone for a week. Most days there is no card.",
            "New: nothing about sleep. No suggestion is ever driven by your sleep, resting pulse, Body Battery, stress or HRV. The rule book reads your morning answers, how hard sessions felt, the minutes planned and done, the days without training, and hikes and walks of 30 minutes or more. The words of every card avoid medical talk.",
            "New: Stop sign and I'm ill. One small pill, Not well?, on Today and at the foot of a session (not beside the heading, so the heading keeps its room) opens a plate with the two, each with one line saying what it does. Stop sign opens a page of fixed words (Stop training now., the signs, that a doctor must look first, and 112 if it is strong) and pauses all suggestions at once, on all your devices. Only the green button A doctor has seen me ends the pause. Opened by mistake takes it back on the same day. I'm ill asks Fever, or chest / body aches? and guides the way back by days: rest until 48 hours symptom-free, two easy days, a week at about half, a week at about three quarters, then the plan as written; a cold above the neck is easy and shorter while it lasts. Symptom-free since and Still not right are there. One grey line on Today says where you are. While paused, or resting after a fever, no card comes at all.",
            "New: Something hurts? Once, under How hard was it?, after a session from today or yesterday: Calf, Achilles, Knee, Other, Nothing hurts. A calf, Achilles or knee may bring a card turning the next easy run into a row, an easy spin or a rest. The app does not say what is wrong.",
            "New: a grey line when your own change goes against the rule book. On the Move and Change pages one calm grey line may say Friday is your rest day., That makes two hard days in a row., That week goes over its planned time. and so on. It never blocks you and never asks. On an iPad or Mac the same line also appears when you drag a session to another day, under the words that say it moved.",
            "New: Settings → Suggestions (under Changes to the plan, once the plan lives in the app). The switch Suggest changes to my plan, which is on until you turn it off; four answers as switches; and What was suggested, a list of every card with your answer in words. Cancel and Save. A card you took is listed in Changes to the plan with its reason, starting Suggestion:, and can be undone there.",
            "Good to know, honestly: only your iPhone makes cards, and only once the plan lives in the app. The notes about cards and your answers are kept on the device where you tapped them. Stop sign and I'm ill are shared through your own iCloud, in a small note of their own beside the plan: a Stop sign tapped on your iPad or Mac pauses your iPhone too, once both have met iCloud. The newest tap counts, but a pause is never ended by an older all clear. With iCloud off, each device keeps its own.",
            "New: Claude built in, optional. Settings → Claude. It is off until you type your own key and switch it on. Claude may only pick one of the choices the rule book already made, and word the reason in one sentence. It cannot add a choice or change your plan. The card appears at once with the rule book's pick and never waits; if a good answer arrives while the card is still open, Claude's pick and reason take its place and a small grey line says Picked by Claude from the rule book's choices. Claude has one try of at most 20 seconds; an answer that comes later, or after you have opened Other choice or touched the card, is not used, so the words never change under your finger.",
            "New: the app checks every answer. A pick outside the menu, a reason that is not one short line starting with Why:, or one that mentions a doctor, injury, medicine, sleep, pulse or HRV, is thrown away and the rule book's own pick stays. The reason must also pass the rule book's own word check, so healthy, fit, safe and your heart are not allowed.",
            "New: what goes to Anthropic, and what does not. For one card: the choices and the rule book's reason, today's date, the last 14 days (minutes planned and done, how hard out of 10, your morning answer from 1 to 5, extras like hike 90 min) and the next 7 days of the plan (sports, minutes, zone words). Not sent: your name, photographs, notes, session names, tests, zones, weight, Garmin or Health numbers, sleep, the race. It goes straight from your iPhone to Anthropic. Your key is kept in the iPhone's password store on this device only, never in iCloud, never in a copy. Remove the key takes it away and switches Claude off. Settings → Claude lists all of this, in full, on the page itself.",
            "New: the monthly cap and the log. The page shows This month: … US dollars of 5.00 and the number of answers. The app stops asking when the month reaches 5 US dollars (checked before each question, so the last answer may go a little over; the count is the app's own estimate). What Claude answered lists the last 30 answers with the time, what was chosen, the reason and the cost.",
            "New: Export for Claude. Share the plan as text gives your season as plain text (phases, tests and zones, the last 8 weeks, the next 4) to paste into the Claude app yourself. It works with no key and sends nothing by itself.",
            "New: a link to two neighbour apps, AMS Workout Companion and AMS Magic Morning Routine, on the same iPhone. It works only once their matching versions are installed. Notes pass through one small shared item in the iPhone's password store, on this iPhone only.",
            "New: the morning answer is taken over. Answer How do you feel? in Magic Morning or Workouts and this app does not ask again. Today shows Feeling good — from Magic Morning (or from Workouts) and under it Answered in Magic Morning — change it there.; it is changed in that app, and if it changes there the same day, this app follows. The five words are Bad, Tired, OK, Good, Great. Answered once, never twice: the first answer of the day wins. An answer taken over counts as your own here, so it goes to iCloud, to the Mornings bars, and into the rule book's reading.",
            "New: strength done in Workouts. On a strength session still to do, a grey line Done in Workouts at 07:40 · 35 min with a small green button Log it. Nothing is logged without your tap; afterwards, Logged from Workouts. A small grey button Open Workouts shows when Workouts is installed.",
            "New: Stretching: 4 of the last 7 mornings, one grey line in the Load card on Progress, from Magic Morning. A count only.",
            "Changed: What this app does not do now says what is true. It still never changes your plan by itself. It no longer says it gives no advice or sends nothing anywhere else: with suggestions on, it suggests changes you may take or keep, and with Claude on, the pieces listed above go to Anthropic. Today's morning paragraph is corrected: your answer is not written into the plan, but it does go to your own iCloud and into the rule book's reading.",
            "Unchanged: logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, Progress, Load, zones, tests, Thursday rides, iCloud, Garmin, the Training calendar and photographs. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "New in How this works: Suggestions by the rule book, Stop sign, I'm ill and Something hurts, Claude built in and Your two neighbour apps are new parts; Today, On a session's page, On iPad and Mac, The same plan on all your devices and What this app does not do say what changed. Signs in this app has the new cards, buttons, lines and words, each with its meaning."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.2 (76)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "iPad and Mac, one plan everywhere, Garmin in the morning", items: [
            "On iPad and Mac. The app now has its own look on a wide screen. The bar along the bottom becomes a list down the left side: Today, Plan, Sessions, Progress, Settings, each word in its own colour. It opens on Today. Tap the row you are already on to come back to its first screen. On a Mac, Command and 1 to 5 choose a row, and Escape is Cancel. The iPhone looks as before.",
            "New on iPad and Mac: Plan, one page for the whole plan. At the top, always, the season: one bar for every week up to the race. Under it a switch, Week · Month · Year, with what is shown and its time (like Week 12 · Build · Easy week, or November 2026, or Season 2026–27) and small green buttons to move along: Previous week, This week, Next week, and the same for months. Under that the view you chose, and your numbers in a column beside it when the window is wide enough, or under it when it is narrower. There is no separate Week page and no separate Season page.",
            "New: the season bars. A taller bar is more planned time and the colour is the phase, cool early and warm near the race. An easy week is pale and says Easy where there is room; a test week says Test. A clear outline stands round the week, or the weeks of the month, you are looking at. A thin green line with the word Today marks today, and the race's flag with its name and date stands at the right. Tap a bar to open that week.",
            "New: Week. The whole week in seven columns, Monday to Sunday. Each session is a card with its sport's colour down the left edge, its name, its length, the green tick when it is done and the red word Missed when you marked it. Tap a card to open the session. An extra you did sits under a thin line in its column, dotted, with the paler tick. When the page is too narrow for seven readable columns, fewer show and you swipe sideways for the others.",
            "New: drag a session to another day, on Week and on Month. Once the plan lives in the app, a session still to do can be dragged onto another day, which gets a blue frame while it is over it. The page says what happened for eight seconds, like Long ride moved to Fri 27 Nov, with an Undo button. It is the same change as Change on the session's page with only the day new, so it also appears in Changes to the plan. A rest day, a done session and a missed one are not moved. There are no arrow buttons, only the drag.",
            "New: + Add at the foot of each day on Week makes a new session on that day.",
            "New: Month. The month as a calendar, one row for every week, with Week 12, Easy week or Test week, the planned time and the time done at the left of each row. Every session is a small chip with its sport's colour, a short name, its length, the green tick or the word Missed. A cell shows three chips at most; with more, +2 more opens that day's week. Days of the neighbouring months are paler, and today says Today in green.",
            "New: Progress uses the whole width. On a wide window (an iPad on its side, the Mac) its cards stand in two columns: left, how the training is working (Is it working?, Fitness and freshness, Load); right, what was done (Twelve weeks, Where the hours went and the counts). On a narrow window they stand in one column as on the iPhone.",
            "New: Year. Every month of the plan as a small block with its planned time and the time done, and a little calendar of squares, one for each day, in the colour of the day's main sport: solid when recorded, pale while still to do, hatched when missed, an empty outline on a rest day, red on race day, a dark frame on today. The key under the blocks says so. On an iPad on its side and on the Mac the whole year fits on the page in two rows of six months. Tap a month to open it. Under it, Phases lists each phase with its colour, its first and last day, its weeks and its hours.",
            "New: your numbers beside the plan. By sport: the time for each sport in what is shown, planned and done. Load, last 12 weeks: twelve small bars and the figures This week and usual. Plan followed: how many of the sessions due by today are done, like 12 of 15 sessions · 80 % (invented numbers), or Nothing due yet. To the race: the weeks left and the date. They are shown, never judged.",
            "The same plan everywhere. Your plan, everything you log and change, and your answers to How do you feel? and How hard was it? are now the same on your iPhone, your iPad and your Mac. They travel through your own iCloud, in a folder of this app, and nowhere else. Each device keeps its own full copy and works without internet; they meet when you open the app, a moment after a change, and about every half minute while it is open.",
            "When two devices changed things while they were apart, they are joined and nothing you logged is lost. A session's plan side (day, sport, words, length) and its log side (what you recorded) each come from the device that changed it last, so a change of plan on the iPad and a log on the iPhone both stay. A session is taken out only on purpose, and a log made later brings it back.",
            "New: a session you logged is never lost to a removal made on another device. If you logged it on a device that had not yet heard that it was taken out, or logged it after it was taken out, it comes back, and Changes to the plan has a line that starts with Came back and says which of the two it was.",
            "New: a device waits for iCloud's list of what is in the folder, up to 20 seconds, before it meets the others for the first time, so a plan that is on its way is never taken for a plan that is not there. If the list has not come, the dot says On its way and nothing is sent. When your other devices already use a plan that has not reached this one, Settings → iCloud says so, in words: Your plan from your iPhone has not reached this iPad yet. Nothing is sent from here until it has.",
            "New: a copy before anything is taken in. Before a device takes in anything from the others, it keeps its own plan as it was. The copies are in Settings → Safety copies, newest first, each with the day, the time and before your Mac's changes came in. The newest 20 are kept, and the copies made when something was taken out of this device's plan are counted apart, so quiet meetings cannot push them out. Without room for a copy, nothing is taken in.",
            "New: words for what a meeting took out. When a meeting took something out of the plan on this device, the green dot's words change from Same on all devices to what happened, like 2 things were taken out by your Mac — see Safety copies. They stay until you have looked at Settings → iCloud or Settings → Safety copies, and then the dot goes back to its usual words. The same words are on the iCloud page.",
            "Changed: Put this copy back on a plan that is shared with another device now works on the plan itself, on all devices: its days, words and lengths, and which sessions are in it go back. What you logged since the copy stays, and so does a session the copy does not have. The question says so before you go on. On a plan that is not shared, everything since the copy is taken out, as before.",
            "New: Settings → iCloud, the first row under Your plan. It shows the dot with its words: green, Same on all devices; amber, On its way; grey, iCloud is off; red, a problem, and the words say which. Then when the devices last met, the button Sync now, Your devices (each iPhone, iPad and Mac with when it was last seen and its version), what is shared, and Copy from before iCloud. The same dot with its words sits at the foot of the side list on iPad and Mac.",
            "New: an iPad or a Mac that opens the app for the first time has no Excel, no Dropbox and nothing to choose. Today says in one line, beside a dot, what it is waiting for: Bringing your plan from iCloud…, or that the plan lives on your iPhone and you should open the app there once, or that it is still in Excel and where to move it in, or how to sign in to iCloud. When the plan arrives it says Plan from your iPhone with a count and the time of the last change, and opens by itself.",
            "New: on an iPhone that is still on Excel, if your iCloud already holds a plan from another device, the page The plan moves in offers the green button Use the plan from iCloud instead of a second import. Anything still waiting on the iPhone is written into that plan. Your Excel file is not changed.",
            "New: two different plans. If your iCloud holds a plan from a second, separate move into the app, the app does not join them. Settings → iCloud shows both side by side, On this iPad and In iCloud, from your iPhone, with their sessions, what is done and the last change, and the button Use this one under each. Choosing the plan on this device keeps it. Choosing the plan from iCloud first asks Use that plan here?, says in words what each plan holds and that the plan on this device will be replaced, and has Cancel and the red button Use that plan here. The plan that is not kept is listed in Settings → Safety copies, where it can be put back; putting one back makes iCloud ask again which plan to keep.",
            "New: if a device's clock is behind, the iCloud page says so in red, so that the newest change always wins. A device running an older Triathlon than the plan says Update Triathlon on this device and changes nothing.",
            "Changed: Settings shows what belongs to each device. On an iPad or a Mac, Your plan says Lives in this app and in iCloud, or Not on this iPad yet while the plan is on its way. Calendar says Kept by your iPhone. Apple Health says From your iPhone on a Mac. Dropbox and its copy are for the iPhone only. Going back to Excel is closed once an iPad or a Mac uses the plan; a spreadsheet copy is then the way out.",
            "Changed: the spreadsheet copy in Dropbox is written by the iPhone only. An iPad or a Mac never writes it, so three devices cannot overwrite one another's copy.",
            "Morning numbers from Garmin. Settings → Garmin: make a personal key once in your Garmin account at connect.garmin.com, paste it into Paste your Garmin key and tap Save (Cancel closes the page). The page then says Connected, when the numbers were last read, and has the buttons Read again now and Remove the key (it asks first). The key is kept in this device's password store, shown only as dots, and is never sent to iCloud or kept in a copy. An iPad or a Mac that should show the numbers needs the key pasted there too.",
            "New on Today: a second morning line with Garmin's numbers, like HRV 64 (+3) · Sleep 7 h 20 · Resting 47 (−1) · Body Battery 71 (invented numbers). HRV and Resting carry how far they sit from your own normal in brackets: green the good way, red the other, grey when it is as usual, or the day your normal will be there. Under it a dot with its words: green, Garmin · this morning, read 07:12; grey, Garmin · older numbers from a day.",
            "New: tap that line for a plate, Garmin, this morning: HRV overnight with Garmin's balanced range, Sleep last night, Resting heart rate, Body Battery on waking and Stress yesterday, each with your normal and how many days it stands on, and when your watch last sent its numbers to Garmin. Done closes it. Where Garmin has a number that Apple Health also has (sleep, HRV, resting), the Garmin one is shown and the Health one is left out, so one thing is never two numbers side by side.",
            "These Garmin numbers are shown only. They never change your plan, and nothing reacts to them: no advice, no score. The app reads them when Today opens, at most once in half an hour; Read again now asks at once. It only reads, and writes nothing to Garmin. (Since 2.17, Garmin strength activities can tick a planned strength session; the numbers still do not.)",
            "Changed on iPad and Mac: the Health numbers are the iPhone's, put in iCloud by the iPhone. They are shown in the same row with a small grey line under it, from iPhone, as of 07:12 (yesterday 07:12 once they are more than 18 hours old, and then paler).",
            "Good to know: the plan has to live in the app on your iPhone first. Until you have moved it in (Settings → Your plan → Move the plan into this app), your iPad and Mac have nothing to fetch. The first time an iPad or a Mac opens the app it waits for the plan, then opens it by itself.",
            "Good to know: what stays on the iPhone. Dropbox and its copy of the plan, the Training calendar (it appears in Calendar on your iPad and Mac through iCloud), and Apple Health. Photographs, the Garmin key and the safety copies stay on the device where they were made. Each device saves its spreadsheet copies in its own Files.",
            "Good to know: nothing is sent anywhere but your own iCloud, and, if you saved a key, from Garmin to your device. Nothing goes to your watch, and the app still says nothing medical.",
            "Good to know: the way back. Every device keeps the plan it had before it first met iCloud, for good: Settings → iCloud → Copy from before iCloud, with a Share button. Spreadsheet copies work as before, and Safety copies now also list the copies kept around iCloud.",
            "Unchanged: logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extras, Progress, Load, zones, tests, Thursday rides, the Training calendar and photographs. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "New in How this works: On iPad and Mac (the Plan page with Week, Month and Year, and your numbers), The same plan on all your devices and Morning numbers from Garmin are new parts; What this app is, Where the plan lives, Today, Changing the plan, How your plan is kept safe, Photographs, Before you train, In your calendar and What this app does not do say what changed. Signs in this app has the new dots and bars, each with its words."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.1 (75)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "Enter a test, safety copies, Thursday rides", items: [
            "New: Enter a test result. Settings → Your zones now lists every test, newest first, with the green button Enter a test result. The main button comes first. Under it are the tests that have numbers, newest first, and one card, Still to come, for the plan's tests without numbers yet. The page has Threshold pulse, Bike power (FTP), Swim pace per 100 m (minutes and seconds, like 1:50), Weight, First day, Last day and Notes. Same as the last test fills the four numbers and leaves days and notes alone. Cancel closes; Save keeps it. Your zones follow the newest numbers at once.",
            "Save never greys out. If something is missing or out of range, a red line above it says what. An empty box means not tested this time; at least one number is needed; the last day cannot be before the first. Ranges: pulse 80 to 220, FTP 50 to 500 W, swim pace 1:00 to 4:00, weight 35 to 150 kg. A grey line says which test the entry becomes: the next one the plan has waiting for numbers, like Saves as Test 3, or a new test if none is waiting.",
            "Changed: Settings → Safety copies is now one row, and it opens the page. A copy is made at the start of each day the plan changes, not every day, and kept for 30 days. Each row gives the day and what its copy holds, like 310 sessions · 64 done · 4 changes so far. With none yet the page says No safety copies yet.",
            "Under each row, a red button, Put this copy back, asks first. The plan goes back to how it was at the start of that day, and everything logged or changed from that day on is taken out. The plan as it is now is kept aside first, so even this step can be put right. Afterwards a green line says The plan is back as it was at the start of that day.",
            "New: Settings → Thursday rides. One easy ride each Thursday, beside the easy run, from the next Monday to the race. 45 minutes in Base 2; growing from 50 to 60 minutes through Base 3; 60 in Build; 45 in Peak. A 30-minute easy spin in easy weeks, test weeks and the taper. None in the race-practice weeks and none in race week.",
            "The page lists every ride, and for each week its time before → after in hours and minutes. Nothing is added until you tap Add 29 rides (the number is the real count). Cancel closes it before; Done after, with a green line: 29 rides added. Undo them under Changes to the plan. A Thursday that already has its ride is skipped; when all are there the page says These rides are already in your plan. If adding fails, a red line says so and nothing is changed. The rides are ordinary sessions afterwards.",
            "New on a session's page: a session over 90 minutes that is still to do carries one grey line about eating and drinking on the way (about 30–60 g of carbohydrate an hour). A strength session, to do or done, carries one about protein afterwards (20–30 g within an hour or two). These are common habits of sport, not medical advice.",
            "New on a session's page: a Garmin card. A run or ride made of repeats, like 3 × 8 min at Z3, carries it while it is still to do. Swims, strength, finished sessions and texts the app cannot read into steps have none. It is one line, Build it like this in Garmin Connect, with a small green button Show the steps (Hide the steps when open). The steps say how to build the workout in Garmin Connect, and Copy the steps copies them as text. Saved there, it stays in your Workouts list: copy it for next week and send it to your watch. The app itself sends nothing to the watch.",
            "Good to know: the test page, the safety copies and the Thursday rides work once the plan lives in the app. The grey lines and the Garmin card show whether the plan is in Excel or in the app.",
            "Unchanged: Today, Sessions, Progress, Load, Apple Health, the Training calendar and photographs. Your Excel file is not touched.",
            "New in How this works: Where the plan lives, Your zones, How your plan is kept safe, Changing the plan, On a session's page and What this app does not do say what is new. Signs in this app has the new marks."
        ]),
        Release(version: "2.0 (74)", date: "25 November 2026", headline: "The plan can live in the app", items: [
            "Big change, and your choice: the plan can now move from the Excel file in Dropbox into this app. Nothing happens until you tap. If you do nothing, the app works as before.",
            "To move it: Settings → Your plan → Move the plan into this app → Start → Take the plan in and count. The app counts the plan as Excel has it and as the app holds it.",
            "Excel and the app, side by side shows both counts for sessions, training, rest days, done, missed, still to come, extra workouts and minutes. Green same: they agree. Red differs: they do not. Month by month shows the same for each month.",
            "Looked odd in the file lists strange things, such as a pace that cannot be. They are taken in as written; correct them later with the pen.",
            "Everything matches. brings the button Make this app the plan's home. Nothing is saved until you tap it. Entries still waiting for Dropbox must be sent first.",
            "After the switch, logging, Missed, Move, Swap, extra workouts and How hard was it? are saved in the app at once, also without internet. Nothing is written into your Excel file any more, and what you change there, the app does not see. Logging follows the same rules as before; it was checked against Excel on the same entries.",
            "Settings → Your plan now says Lives in this app, with the day you moved it. Safety copies: one for each day the plan changed, the newest 30 kept.",
            "Spreadsheet copy: Save a copy now makes a spreadsheet of the plan, to keep or send. The app also makes one about once a week in Files → On My iPhone → Triathlon, and keeps the newest eight. Each is checked against the plan first; one that does not match is never given.",
            "Copy in Dropbox: the app also saves the plan there as a spreadsheet, Triathlon plan from the app, beside your Excel file. It is written a little after each change and never read back. Settings → Your plan → Copy in Dropbox shows when.",
            "Go back to Excel: for three weeks a red button writes the plan into your Excel file in Dropbox and makes Excel the plan's home again. If that file changed in the meantime, the app refuses and does nothing. After three weeks the button goes.",
            "New, once the plan lives in the app: on a session's page, Change opens Change session (Day, Sport, What you do, Length in minutes, Zone or effort, Purpose, Key session; Cancel and Save) with a red Take out of the plan. On the Sessions tab, + Session opens New session.",
            "Settings → Changes to the plan lists every change, newest first, with Before and Now and an Undo button. A change that is undone stays in the list, marked Undone. Only the newest change to a session can be undone; an older one says Changed again since. It never undoes what you logged. A session keeps its photographs, its place in the Training calendar and its move history.",
            "Unchanged: Today, Sessions, Progress, the two questions, Load, Apple Health, the Training calendar and photographs work as before, with the plan in Excel or in the app.",
            "Good to know: a spreadsheet copy does not change after it is made. Until the iPad and Mac versions come, the plan lives on this iPhone only. Your iPhone's own iCloud copy includes it, and so do the safety copies.",
            "Fixed: tapping a tab at the bottom now changes the page at once. It used to slide, and after adding a session the pages could stop half-way between two tabs. Swiping is unchanged.",
            "New: How this works has two new parts, Where the plan lives and Changing the plan. Every other part says what holds before and after the switch. Signs in this app explains the new marks.",
            "Checked before release: the move was rehearsed on a copy of a real plan, every session and every month compared, and a team of reviewers tried to break it. What they found was fixed first: a change is shown only once it is safely saved, a plan that will not open is put back from its newest safety copy, and the Excel file is read once more at the moment you tap the switch.",
            "Coming next, with no dates: the app on iPad and Mac, a morning check with Garmin numbers, suggestions by the rule book, Claude built in, and links to Workout Companion and Magic Morning."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.2 (73)", date: "24 November 2026", headline: "A new name, how you feel, how hard it was, and your load", items: [
            "New name: AMS Triathlon Training. Under the icon on the home screen it reads Triathlon. It is the same app with the same data, and nothing to set up again. This is the first step of growing the app into one training app. The plan still lives in your Excel file, untouched.",
            "Today asks a morning question, How do you feel? A small card under the green heading shows five faces with a word under each: Bad, Tired, OK, Good, Great. One tap, once a day. After the tap the card is gone until tomorrow, and the morning line shows Feeling good (or the word you chose). Tap that word to change it. The answer is kept on this phone only; it is not written into the plan. Nothing on Today reacts to it: no advice, no score.",
            "After Done, the session asks How hard was it? On the session's own page, where the Done button was, there is now a row of numbers 1 to 10 (1 very easy, 7 hard, 10 all out). One tap saves it into the plan's Effort column, the same box as Effort in Log details, so there is no new column in Excel. If you do not answer, it simply waits on that session: no reminder, no badge. Extra workouts get the same row on their own page.",
            "Progress has a new Load card, directly under Fitness and freshness. It shows three figures: this week so far, last week, and your usual week, which is the average of the four finished weeks before this one. Under them are eight weekly bars.",
            "Load is minutes times how hard it was (1 to 10): a 60-minute run at 5 counts 300. A solid purple bar is sessions in the plan. A dotted purple bar is outside the plan: your extra workouts (all of them except breathing and meditation), and workouts in Apple Health that are in neither the plan nor your extras (hikes, the gym), if they are at least 10 minutes long. Breathing and meditation are left out.",
            "Where no number was given, the app uses the plan's zone (Z1 counts 2, Z2 counts 3, Z3 counts 5, Z4 counts 7, Z5 counts 9), and where there is no zone it counts 3, which is easy. The card says how many were guessed. Health workouts of the last 14 days without a number are listed there with a How hard? button; that answer is kept on the phone.",
            "A row of fourteen small bars, Mornings, shows how you felt each morning. Taller is better. A gap means you did not answer.",
            "The app only shows. It suggests nothing and changes nothing in the plan by itself. Sleep is shown and never leads to advice.",
            "Fixed: a rest day now carries a moon. It used to carry the same tick as done, which was wrong: the tick means done and nothing else.",
            "New in How this works: Signs in this app, every mark and colour and what it means. Also a short part, What this app does not do.",
            "New: a written specification of the whole app is kept with the code.",
            "Tidied: two stray copies of the project file were removed from the code store. Nothing you can see.",
            "Unchanged: your Excel plan and your zones. No new test numbers were entered in November, so the zones stay on the last test until the next one."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (72)", date: "28 October 2026", headline: "The trend is always there, in brackets", items: [
            "Resting and HRV now always carry their trend in brackets — Resting 48 (−2) — green when it moved the good way, red when the other, grey when it is about as usual. Before, the figure was left out whenever the difference was small, so a quiet morning looked like a missing trend.",
            "Your normal is worked out more carefully. It used to average every reading Health held over the fortnight, this morning's included, so a day Health held twice counted twice and the morning was partly measured against itself. Now each day counts once, the morning shown is held against the days before it, and there is no normal until four days are there to make one — the brackets say \"normal in 2 days\" until then.",
            "Settings → Apple Health → What Health hands over shows your normal beside each reading and how many days it stands on, and says sleep is \"none since 6 pm yesterday\" when Garmin has not handed last night over yet."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (71)", date: "27 October 2026", headline: "Slept counts the night once", items: [
            "Slept said 10h 40m after a night of about 5h 20m. Apple Health can hold the same night more than once — Garmin handing it over again on a later sync, or the whole night and its phases side by side — and the app added every copy together. A stretch of sleep now counts once however many times Health holds it, and if two devices both recorded the night, the app takes the fuller of the two rather than adding them."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (70)", date: "27 October 2026", headline: "The morning line is one row, always current — and a Dropbox button", items: [
            "The morning line at the top of Today is a single row now — Slept 7h 24m, Resting 48 −2, HRV 64 +6 — instead of three stacked readings. The small figure after a reading is how far it sits from your own fortnight: green where that way is the good way, grey otherwise, nothing at all when it is as usual.",
            "Today read your night once, the first time the screen appeared, and never again until the app was closed and reopened — so a first read that found nothing left the line missing until a visit to Settings forced a second one. It now reads again every time you open the app.",
            "The line sits right under the heading instead of floating below it.",
            "Without Dropbox, Today used to say Read only in a pill — which looked like a button and gave you nothing to press. It is a real button now: Connect Dropbox, or Choose your plan if Dropbox is connected but no plan is picked, and it takes you to Settings. On your phone it does not show while Dropbox is connected."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (69)", date: "27 October 2026", headline: "Settings says what Health has for the night", items: [
            "Settings → Apple Health → What Health hands over now lists sleep, resting heart rate and HRV, each as a value or as none in Health. Today hides the morning line when it has nothing to show, which left no way to tell not allowed from nothing there; this is the place to look.",
            "Garmin passes sleep to Apple Health once you switch it on in Garmin Connect (Settings → Connected Apps → Apple Health). It does not appear to pass on HRV, and resting heart rate is not confirmed — so some of the three may stay empty however much you allow."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (68)", date: "26 October 2026", headline: "Health is asked for the morning numbers", items: [
            "The line at the top of Today never appeared. The app had permission to read your workouts, granted weeks ago, and iOS treats every kind of data as a permission of its own: nothing ever put the question for sleep, resting heart rate and HRV, so the app read a drawer it had never been given the key to and said nothing. It now asks iOS whether the question still needs putting, and puts it — once, for those three."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (67)", date: "13 October 2026", headline: "What a session cost, and what the night left behind", items: [
            "Progress has a new card, Fitness and freshness. Until now the app counted hours, and hours cannot tell an easy week from a hard one: your plan could be kept to the letter and still not be trained. Each session now costs something — an hour at your threshold heart rate is 100, an easy hour far less — and six weeks of those costs is fitness, the last week is fatigue, and what is left of one after the other says whether you are carrying work or rested.",
            "It is worked out from your own heart rate where you recorded it, your effort where you did not, and the zone the plan asked for failing both; the card says so, because an estimate should admit what it is. Heart rate reads low in water, so a swim costs modestly.",
            "Today opens with last night: how long you slept, your resting heart rate and your HRV, each against your own fortnight rather than anybody else's. Three plain numbers and no invented score. Apple Health will ask once for permission to read them."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (66)", date: "13 October 2026", headline: "Tomorrow's card carries its pictures too", items: [
            "Today draws photographs on today's sessions, on today's extra workouts and on anything behind you not recorded — but the block for tomorrow was the one list that did not, so a session done early and photographed showed none of them."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (65)", date: "13 October 2026", headline: "Your photographs come back", items: [
            "Pictures that had stopped being shown are shown again, on Today, in the Sessions list and on the session itself. A photograph remembered the row of the sheet it was taken against, and a row number is not a name: insert a line in Excel and everything below it shifts, so the picture was looking for a row that had become somebody else's. It now falls back on the day and the sport, which shifting rows do not change.",
            "Nothing was ever lost — the pictures were on the phone the whole time, only unfindable."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (64)", date: "12 October 2026", headline: "A bar under the four counts", items: [
            "Under Upcoming, Done, Missed and All there is now one bar for the whole plan: solid for what is recorded, hatched for what was missed, light for what is still to come — the same three signs the week strip on Today uses, in this tab's blue.",
            "It is counted from the same lists the four numbers are counted from, so the picture and the figures cannot disagree. Rest days are in none of them: they are not sessions anybody does."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (63)", date: "12 October 2026", headline: "+1 moves it to tomorrow", items: [
            "The Move sheet carries a +1 beside its heading: one tap and the session is on tomorrow, without the date wheel. It is the move made most often.",
            "Move the session is never a dead grey button any more. Pressed before you have picked another day it simply waits, and the line underneath says what it wants.",
            "The Extra workout pill sits level with the word TOMORROW instead of a few points below it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (62)", date: "2 October 2026", headline: "Each phase carries its own number", items: [
            "Inside every block of the phase bar, small, the number of sessions that phase holds. The two short blocks near the race — Peak and Taper — have no room for a figure, and their counts are in the list behind the flag.",
            "Today's line used to be drawn straight through the number of the phase you are in. The number now sits to whichever side of the line has more room."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (61)", date: "2 October 2026", headline: "The weekly figures wait for the week to finish", items: [
            "Twelve weeks counts only weeks that are over. A week still being lived showed every session not yet done as time missed, so a Thursday reading had you behind on hours you still had the weekend to do.",
            "Its columns are the weeks that hold training. Nine empty weeks from before the plan began used to be drawn too, squeezing the real ones into the corner with dates printed under nothing — and the last date was cut off at \"21…\". The dates are spaced evenly now, each under its own column, and the line for the hours asked for is the width of the column it belongs to.",
            "On the road card, all three figures stay on one line; 327h 23m used to fold onto a second while the others did not.",
            "Under the phase you are in: how many of its sessions are behind you. In the list behind the flag, each phase now says how many sessions it holds as well as how many weeks it lasts."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (60)", date: "2 October 2026", headline: "What Health hands over opens, it does not switch on", items: [
            "That row carries a chevron now, turning to point down when it is open — the sign for showing and hiding a piece of reading. It was a switch for three builds, and a switch means turning something on: sitting directly under In use and Stop, it read as if it controlled Apple Health itself. It never did."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (59)", date: "2 October 2026", headline: "The open tab fills its whole quarter", items: [
            "The tab you are on is a block of its own colour filling its quarter of the bar — the full width of it, from the top edge down to the bottom of the phone — instead of a small rounded button floating in the middle of it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (58)", date: "2 October 2026", headline: "The extras lose their dots", items: [
            "An extra workout in the week strip is its dotted outline and nothing inside it: the line of dots down the middle is gone, as you asked. The key shows the same."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (57)", date: "1 October 2026", headline: "The phases have colours and names", items: [
            "The phase bar on Progress is no longer four greys: each phase has its own colour, cool at the start of the season and warm towards the race, so the bar reads at a glance. Today's phase is at full strength, the ones behind you and ahead of you a little lighter.",
            "The bar used to run out of its card on the right. Your sheet has a four-week postseason after race day, and the bar is measured in days to the race, so the blocks came to more than the whole road. It stops at the race now, and a phase that falls after it says so instead of giving a length.",
            "The flag beside the weeks to go now also lists the phases under the race: the colour, the name your sheet gives it, and how many weeks long it is. The bar had nothing to say what its blocks were.",
            "Tap the tab you are already on and it goes back to that tab's own first screen — out of a session, out of a list, without pressing Back.",
            "What Health hands over is a switch now rather than a button."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (56)", date: "1 October 2026", headline: "Nothing left that can bring it down", items: [
            "The last places where an unexpected answer from the phone or the network would have stopped the app now stop only what they were doing — the calendar's dates, the sign-in address, a time zone.",
            "Four more tests of how an extra workout reaches your sheet: it lands on the first empty row and never over one in use, it reads back as itself, sending it twice does not double it, and a correction writes only the boxes you altered."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (55)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Disconnect tells you what is still waiting", items: [
            "Settings → Dropbox now says how many entries are still to be sent before you disconnect. They stay on this phone either way, but nothing reaches Dropbox until you connect and choose the plan again."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (54)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "The pictures, not a camera", items: [
            "On Today, a session or an extra with photographs shows them — up to three, in the corner of its card — instead of a camera and a number. The Sessions list already did; Today had been left behind."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (53)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Your waiting logging cannot go missing", items: [
            "Anything logged but not yet sent to Dropbox lives in one file on this phone. If that file could not be read — which an app update could have caused on its own — the app used to start with an empty queue and say nothing. It now reads what it can, keeps a copy of anything it cannot, and tells you.",
            "A record written by an older version of the app reads correctly, with the numbers you put in it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (52)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Hardening: nothing new, less to go wrong", items: [
            "A date the sheet cannot mean — a thirteenth month, a 31st of February — is refused instead of quietly becoming another day. A garbled date in the Extras sheet used to place the row in the wrong week.",
            "The part of the app that talks to Dropbox can no longer be brought down by an odd answer from the network: every such case now fails the sync, with a reason, instead of the app.",
            "Twenty-four new tests of the reading and writing itself, run on every push beside the ones that drive the screens. They already found the date fault above."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (51)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Plainer week, plainer words", items: [
            "A session still to do is a lighter block of its sport's colour in the week strip, with no frame around it.",
            "Extra activity is Extra workout, everywhere the app says it.",
            "Counts as training is a mark now instead of the words — the same little blocks the week bar draws that time in. A workout that does not count carries nothing.",
            "A photograph added while the form is open no longer meets \"nothing has changed\": pictures are kept the moment you add one, so the button simply says Done and closes.",
            "How this works has been brought up to date: the Sessions tab and its four lists, the pen on a row, photographs behind the pen, what Apple Health hands over, and the extra workouts' own marks."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (50)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Mend it from the list", items: [
            "Every session and extra already done carries its pen in the list itself, so a typo is corrected without opening it first.",
            "Beside the pen, up to three of that session's photographs, pen-sized.",
            "Photographs are added behind the pen now, not from the screen at rest — and by one button instead of two: Add photo asks whether to take one or pick from your photos."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (49)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Three things he pointed at", items: [
            "Each tab keeps its own colour whether it is open or not, and the open one sits on a patch of that colour.",
            "What kind of thing is a proper box now, carrying the activity's own badge in its own colour instead of a bare green word.",
            "A session still to do has no frame around it. Done and missed still say so with one.",
            "On an extra's own screen the pen is a round button inside the card, in the bottom corner under the tick."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (48)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Every extra activity has its own icon", items: [
            "Yoga sits cross-legged, Walk walks, Hike carries a pack and a pole, Ski stands on its skis — drawn in the same hand as the swim, the bike, the run and the weight, and no longer borrowing them.",
            "In Settings, Read Health again says what it does, and Ask iOS for access only appears when nothing at all is coming through — there is no reason for it the rest of the time."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (47)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Health works again", items: [
            "Apple Health could not be read at all since build 40: the upload left out the app's HealthKit permission, so iOS refused every question and the app looked as if Health had nothing. It is back, and the upload now refuses to send a build that lacks it.",
            "The extra-activity blocks sit lower, clear of the week's hairline.",
            "A card's small labels stay on one line each and take the next row when they run out of width. Three of them — a length, Counts as training and Waiting to sync — used to squeeze until \"Counts as training\" stood three words high."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (46)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Rowing is a rowing machine", items: [
            "The Rowing icon is the machine itself — fan, rail, seat and the monitor on its arm — drawn by hand like the rest. The crossed oars are gone: shown at the size the app actually draws them, without a label, they said nothing.",
            "Chosen by looking: six candidates in the card they live in, no names, and the one that was recognised won."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (45)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Health says why", items: [
            "Under What Health hands over there is now a line saying when Health was last asked, how many workouts it gave for the last seven days, and whether it gives anything at all. If Health returned an error it is printed in red — the app used to throw that error away, which is why a refusal and an empty day looked the same.",
            "Ask again always leaves something new on screen, and beside it Ask iOS again puts the permission question to iOS once more."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (44)", date: "30 September 2026", headline: "Health, today and yesterday", items: [
            "Settings → Apple Health has a toggle, What Health hands over. It opens two lists: what Apple Health has today, and what Apple Health had yesterday — because yesterday is usually the day in question, and a list that knew only about today said \"nothing\" on a rest morning.",
            "Both lists empty while your watch has something means the app is not being given it: Health → your picture → Apps → Triathlon, switch the rows on, then Ask again."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (43)", date: "29 September 2026", headline: "Health hands over everything it has", items: [
            "A session's form now offers every workout Apple Health holds for that day, the matching sport first. It used to show only the ones whose sport agreed, and say there was nothing at all otherwise — so a run Health had filed as another kind of workout was invisible, and the day looked empty.",
            "Settings → Apple Health lists what Health hands over for today. iOS never tells an app whether reading was allowed, so a refused read looks exactly like an empty day; this line tells the two apart. If it says nothing while your watch has something, open Health → your picture → Apps → Workout Sync and switch the rows on."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (42)", date: "29 September 2026", headline: "Rowing, and the four lists stay put", items: [
            "Rowing is an extra activity of its own, after Strength, with its own oars and its own teal — and it counts as training unless you say otherwise. A rowing workout from Garmin fills its form like any other.",
            "On Sessions, the four words — Upcoming, Done, Missed, All — stay at the top while the list scrolls under them.",
            "Save is never a dead grey button. Pressed before there is anything to save, it says what it wants; it used to go quietly nowhere, which is how a walk could look saved and not be.",
            "When Apple Health is switched off or not yet connected, the form says so and offers to put it back on. Before, it simply showed nothing and looked broken.",
            "An extra that counts always draws at least one block under the week bar; under eight minutes it used to draw none.",
            "The week's key explains the blocks: only extras marked as counting are in them."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (41)", date: "27 September 2026", headline: "Extra activities have their own bar", items: [
            "Under the week's hairline on Today there is now a second row: one block for each quarter hour of extra activity that counts as training, every fourth block in amber, so a yellow block is an hour done. Extras stay out of the week's figures, as before — this is beside the plan, never inside it.",
            "An extra marked as not training load adds nothing to it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (40)", date: "23 September 2026", headline: "The pen sits with the numbers", items: [
            "The pen is on the What you did line, beside the figures it edits. On a session logged a moment ago, which has no figures until it syncs, it stays under the card so it is never out of reach."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (38)", date: "23 September 2026", headline: "A pen instead of the word", items: [
            "Adjust is a small grey button carrying a hand-drawn pen, with no word on it, on a logged session and on an extra. It still says Adjust logged data aloud for VoiceOver."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (37)", date: "23 September 2026", headline: "The same app, sent a new way", items: [
            "Nothing in the app itself changed. This build was sent to TestFlight by GitHub rather than from the Mac, to prove that path works — so a change made while the Mac is off can still reach your phone."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (36)", date: "22 September 2026", headline: "One row of buttons, your words further up, and marks for breathing and meditation", items: [
            "On a session still to do, all four buttons are now one row at one size: Done (with the planned length on it), Log details, Missed, Move. Done keeps its green fill — it is still the one that finishes the session — but it no longer takes the whole screen.",
            "On a session you have logged, your note is shown directly under the figures, above the photographs, instead of below everything.",
            "Breathing extras carry a pair of lungs and meditation extras a lotus, both hand-drawn, instead of a tick — which, beside the done tick every extra now carries, made two ticks on one card.",
            "A long note on a logged session is shown in full; its last line used to be cut off. And at night the grey of breathing, meditation and rest is lighter, so their names and marks can be read."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (35)", date: "22 September 2026", headline: "Garmin for extras too", items: [
            "An extra activity's form now offers the day's workouts from Apple Health, as a session's form does — for a new extra and when you adjust a saved one. Use fills the time, the distance and the heart rate; a new extra also takes the workout's kind. Nothing is saved until you press Save.",
            "An extra's card carries the done tick everywhere it appears — Today, Sessions under Done and All, Settings, its own screen — in the paler green the week strip gives extras.",
            "An extra's own screen shows the same small grey Adjust as a logged session, instead of a green button."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (34)", date: "22 September 2026", headline: "Extras: corrected, listed under Done, ticked", items: [
            "An extra activity can be changed after it is saved. Open it — from Today, from Sessions under Done, or from Settings → Extra activities — and press Adjust. The form opens filled in with what the sheet holds, and only the boxes you change are written into its own row; the button counts them before you press it. A box you empty empties the cell.",
            "Extras are now listed on the Sessions tab under Done and under All, in the day they happened, beside that day's sessions. They used to be on Today for a day and after that only under Settings.",
            "Each extra in the week strip carries the same small tick as a done session, in a paler green — it is something you did, and it is still not part of the plan."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (33)", date: "21 September 2026", headline: "Extra activity on the Tomorrow line", items: [
            "The Extra activity button is a small pill on the Tomorrow line, beside the blue Tomorrow tab on the page's own ground, instead of a full-width row of its own. On a day with no Tomorrow block it sits alone on the right."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (32)", date: "21 September 2026", headline: "The pace is yours; done bars carry a tick", items: [
            "Use from Apple Health fills time, distance and heart rate, and no longer works out a pace or a speed. Garmin's own pace is not in Apple Health, and a sum from the whole session was wrong for any workout with rest in it: a 1:56 swim came out as 3:39. Type the pace from Garmin Connect.",
            "Each done session in the week strip carries a small green tick, the same sign as on a done session card."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (31)", date: "21 September 2026", headline: "Swim pace as Garmin shows it", items: [
            "The swim pace filled in from Apple Health counted the rest between sets as swimming: a 1:56 swim came out as 3:39. It now uses only the time you were actually swimming — the lengths, or failing those the watch's laps and pauses — as Garmin does.",
            "A swim already saved with the wrong pace: open it, press Adjust, then Use on the Garmin swim, and Save — only the pace changes."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (30)", date: "21 September 2026", headline: "A logged session stops asking", items: [
            "Once a session is logged, Missed and Move are gone: they no longer apply. A small grey Adjust stays for fixing a typo.",
            "Logged with one tap and your Garmin workout is in Apple Health? A small Fill from Garmin stays until the watch's numbers are in, then it goes too. The app knows they are in when you used them in the form, or when the recorded time and distance match the watch's.",
            "On a session still to do, Done as planned stays the one big button; Log details, Missed and Move are small, in one row.",
            "The week's hours on Today now add up the time you actually recorded — a 47-minute swim counts 47 — instead of each done session's planned length. Only a session marked done without a time still counts as planned."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (29)", date: "20 September 2026", headline: "The four disciplines along the bottom", items: [
            "The tab bar now carries the sports: swim for Today, bike for Sessions, run for Progress, strength for Settings. The words are unchanged, and each icon still takes its page's colour."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (28)", date: "20 September 2026", headline: "One size of button in Settings", items: [
            "Every button on the Settings screen is now the same size, and it is the small one: the full-width buttons for choosing the plan and connecting Dropbox are gone.",
            "Settings → Calendar can put the sessions in as all-day events instead of at an hour. Choose At a time or All day; everything from today onwards changes over."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (27)", date: "20 September 2026", headline: "Four small things you asked for", items: [
            "Under the week's hours on Today: a hairline showing how much of the planned time is recorded, with a faint notch where the week stands once tonight is done.",
            "Tomorrow sits on its own pale blue ground, so the eye knows at once that everything below it is no longer today.",
            "Sessions shows how many are upcoming, done and missed, the number under each word.",
            "Progress no longer carries the race description. It is behind the small flag beside the weeks: tap it for the race's own words, tap again and it goes.",
            "Settings is quieter: Read it again now is a small grey line under Change, and what the app made of your sheet is one grey line instead of a section. The photo buttons are small.",
            "Your zones now read your latest test's own numbers, so they show even when the file has lost what Excel worked out. When the zone tables themselves are empty, the app says why and what to do about it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (26)", date: "18 September 2026", headline: "Short headings in the calendar", items: [
            "A calendar event is now headed by the sport and its length and nothing else: Run 35, Swim 40, Bike 2h30min. The session's own words are still there, in the event's notes. Events from today onwards are rewritten the next time the app opens; days already behind keep the heading they had."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (25)", date: "16 September 2026", headline: "Red where something is taken away", items: [
            "Stop under Apple Health and Take them out under Calendar are red now, like Disconnect and Discard: every button that takes something away is red, every other one green."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (24)", date: "16 September 2026", headline: "Zones, the calendar, and sending a session", items: [
            "Tap a session's Z2 or Z4–Z5 and the app says what that is for you — heart rate, bike power, swim paces — from the Test Results & Zones sheet of your workbook, from your latest test. The whole sheet is under Settings → Your zones.",
            "Settings → Calendar → Put them in keeps every session from today onwards in a Training calendar, at the hour you set and as long as it is planned, and keeps the events right when sessions move.",
            "The share button on a session sends the whole session, or, once it is done, what you did, with its photos.",
            "How this works no longer points at the web app: the phone app is the app."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (23)", date: "16 September 2026", headline: "Bike and strength told apart", items: [
            "The bike's yellow is brighter and the strength orange stronger, so the two no longer look alike in the week bars and on the badges. The web app uses the same two colours from v1.72.2. (Build 22 carried a quieter version of the same change.)"
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (21)", date: "16 September 2026", headline: "The wave is back", items: [
            "The app icon is the green training wave on dark teal again — the web app's icon, redrawn with one even stroke, equal peaks and round corners. The calendar from build 20 is gone."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.1 (20)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Progress", items: [
            "The Progress tab, as in the web app: the road to the race with the phases as one bar, is it working (distance per heartbeat, then against now), twelve weeks against what they asked for, where the hours went by sport, and what was kept — consistency, the sport that runs behind, missed or moved. Every figure checked against the web app's on the same workbooks: no differences.",
            "Moves made in this app are remembered on this phone for the missed-or-moved figure, as the web app remembers its own.",
            "A new app icon (replaced again in build 21).",
            "Swipe reaches Progress like the other pages."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.0 (19)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Tomorrow, not the next three", items: [
            "Under today's sessions, Today now shows only tomorrow's — a rest day included — instead of the next three sessions."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.0 (18)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Swipe between the screens", items: [
            "Today, Sessions and Settings are pages: swipe left or right to move between them, or tap the bar as before.",
            "The date is gone from the top of Today — it is always today — and the room went to the week and the sessions."
        ]),
        Release(version: "1.0 (17)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "The AMS Workout Sync app", items: [
            "From today this is the primary Workout Sync: one-tap, the log form, corrections, missed, move and swap, extra activities, photographs and Apple Health, all writing into your plan exactly as the web app did — proven on 651 scenarios, then on your own plan.",
            "The web app stays for the Progress tab, spoken logging and the Mac. Both write to the same plan and check Dropbox's version first, so they can be used side by side."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.5 (16)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Next 3 sessions", items: [
            "Coming up on Today is always the next three sessions, so it says so."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.5 (15)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "A Key button on the week card", items: [
            "The word beside This week is a small button now. Tapping the card still works too."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.5 (14)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Colours and shapes in Settings", items: [
            "The key — recorded, still to do, missed, extra, rest day, and each sport's colour — is now always in Settings as well as one tap away on the This week card."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.5 (13)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Plan is now Sessions", items: [
            "The middle tab holds every session in every state — upcoming, done, missed, all — and two of those are the past, so \"Plan\" was the wrong word for it. Sessions, as you chose."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.5 (12)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Photographs", items: [
            "A session or an extra can carry photographs, from the library or the camera, shrunk to a size a phone can hold a season of. Tap one to see it full size, share it or delete it.",
            "They stay on this phone — never in the workbook, never in Dropbox — and the iPhone's own backup includes them. Settings → Photos saves them all out as a zip, or brings in the zip the web app's Save them all makes, so your pictures from there come across.",
            "A photograph is never shown against a session whose sport no longer matches its row; it is still counted and still exported."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.4 (11)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "A heart on the button, the week key, and a warning", items: [
            "The log button carries a small heart and the word Garmin when Apple Health holds a workout for that day and sport — the numbers are one tap away inside.",
            "Tap the This week card and it explains its own drawing: recorded, still to do, missed, extra, rest day, and the sport colours.",
            "If logging has waited a full day to reach Dropbox, Today says so at the top, with the reason and a Send it now button. Silent below that."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.4 (10)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Stop using Apple Health", items: [
            "Settings → Apple Health has a Stop button: the app then never asks Health for anything again, and Use again turns it back on. iOS does not let an app give its own permission back, so the permission itself is taken away in the Health app — the row says where, and opens it for you."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.4 (9)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "How this works, and What's new", items: [
            "This guide and this list, as the web app has them.",
            "Read it again now is a button."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.4 (8)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Apple Health", items: [
            "The log form offers the day's workouts from Apple Health — your Garmin sends them there — and Use fills duration, distance, heart rate and pace. Nothing is saved until you press Save. Health is only read, never written.",
            "The tag at the top of Today now says something only when there is something to say: Sending…, N waiting, or TEST COPY."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.3 (7)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Extra activities", items: [
            "Walks, yoga, breathing and anything else outside the plan, written to the Extras sheet exactly as the web app writes them — the sheet is created if the workbook has none.",
            "Settings tidied: one way to choose the plan, small buttons on the rows they act on."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.2 (6)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "Missed, Move and Swap", items: [
            "Missed with an optional note. Move to a date. Swap with a nearby session — only sessions still to do are offered, and a move never hides that a session is done."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.2 (5)", date: "15 September 2026", headline: "The log form", items: [
            "How did it go? for a session still to do; Adjust logged data, opening filled in, for one already recorded. Only the boxes you change are written."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.2 (4)", date: "14 September 2026", headline: "The first write from the iPhone", items: [
            "Done as planned. Every write goes through a writer proven to produce exactly the file the web app produces, over 513 scenarios on your own plans."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.1 (3)", date: "14 September 2026", headline: "Dropbox", items: [
            "Connect Dropbox and choose the plan inside it."
        ]),
        Release(version: "0.1 (1)", date: "14 September 2026", headline: "Read only", items: [
            "Today, Plan and a session's details, read from the plan in Files. Reading proven identical to the web app on every session of the plan."
        ])
    ]

    var body: some View {
        ScrollView {
            VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 18) {
                ForEach(Self.releases) { r in
                    VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 8) {
                        HStack(alignment: .firstTextBaseline) {
                            // The date right beside the version, never at the far edge.
                            Text(r.version).font(.headline).foregroundStyle(Theme.text)
                            Text(r.date).font(.caption).foregroundStyle(Theme.secondary)
                            Spacer(minLength: 0)
                        }
                        Text(r.headline).font(.subheadline.weight(.semibold)).foregroundStyle(Theme.today)
                        ForEach(r.items, id: \.self) { item in
                            Text(item).font(.body).foregroundStyle(Theme.text)
                        }
                    }
                    .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading)
                    .padding(14)
                    .background(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 14, style: .continuous).fill(Theme.surface))
                }
            }
            .padding(16).padding(.bottom, 32)
        }
        .background(Theme.bg.ignoresSafeArea())
        .navigationTitle("What's new")
        .navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)
    }
}
